{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PYB3cixyGuKzzN79kRmY2y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/config.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Demo-application–facing configuration plumbing for quic-core:\n4\t//! the [`Config`] bag of CLI-derived options, the [`OptionId`]\n5\t//! tag identifying each option, and [`Config::create_and_configure`],\n6\t//! the one-shot constructor that turns a populated config into a\n7\t//! fully-wired [`Quic`].\n8\t//!\n9\t//! Phase 4: all function bodies are implemented.\n10\t//!\n11\t//! Pointer-shape decisions for the config struct were guided by\n12\t//! reading `quic/config.c`:\n13\t//!\n14\t//! * Every `char const*` string field that\n15\t//!   `config_clear` `free`s is owned in C (allocated via\n16\t//!   `config_set_string_param`'s `malloc` + `memcpy`).  These map\n17\t//!   to `Option<String>`; `None` substitutes for the C `NULL`\n18\t//!   sentinel that all callers test before use.\n19\t//! * `multipath_alt_config: *mut char` is owned the same way and\n20\t//!   becomes `Option<String>`.\n21\t//! * `ech_target: uint8_t*` plus `ech_target_len` is owned by the\n22\t//!   config (`config_clear` frees it after the base64\n23\t//!   decode in `option_ECH_client`); it becomes\n24\t//!   `Option<Vec<u8>>` with the length implicit in the vector.\n25\t//! * `ticket_encryption_key: const uint8_t*` is *borrowed* in C —\n26\t//!   `config_clear` does not free it.  Phase 1 stores an\n27\t//!   owned `Option<Vec<u8>>` for safety; in v1 only the demo apps\n28\t//!   set this field, and they can supply an owned buffer.  Phase 3\n29\t//!   may revisit if a caller actually relies on aliasing.  The\n30\t//!   paired `ticket_encryption_key_length` field is dropped — its\n31\t//!   value is always implicit in the Vec length.\n32\t//! * Single-bit `unsigned int : 1` flag bitfields (`use_long_log`,\n33\t//!   `do_retry`, …) collapse to individual `bool` fields.  Every C\n34\t//!   call site reads/writes one bit at a time as a Boolean\n35\t//!   (`config->do_retry = 1`), so the\n36\t//!   integer-with-mask-and-shift translation buys nothing here and\n37\t//!   `bitflags!` is overkill for an unrelated set of flags.\n38\t//! * Bitfield `enable_sslkeylog` is gated by\n39\t//!   `#ifndef WITHOUT_SSLKEYLOG` in C.  v1 follows the\n40\t//!   canonical build (the macro is undefined), so the field is\n41\t//!   always present in Rust; a `cfg`-gated variant lands when the\n42\t//!   build options are translated.\n43\t\n44\tuse crate::Error;\n45\tuse crate::Instant;\n46\tuse crate::internal::MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX;\n47\tuse crate::{LossbitVersion, Quic, SpinbitVersion, StreamDataCallback};\n48\t\n49\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n50\t// Option identifiers.\n51\t\n52\t/// One identifier per CLI / API option understood by [`Config`].\n53\t///\n54\t/// Mirrors the C `picoquic_option_enum_t`; variant order is\n55\t/// load-bearing — the option dispatch table in `quic/config.c`\n56\t/// indexes by variant — so the discriminants do not get reordered.\n57\t///\n58\t/// [`OptionId::SslKeyLog`] is unconditional here even though the C\n59\t/// enum gates it on `#ifndef WITHOUT_SSLKEYLOG`, matching the\n60\t/// canonical-build behavior; see the module-level docs for the\n61\t/// rationale.\n62\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n63\tpub enum OptionId {\n64\t    Cert,\n65\t    Key,\n66\t    ServerPort,\n67\t    ProposedVersion,\n68\t    OutDir,\n69\t    WwwDir,\n70\t    MaxConnections,\n71\t    DoRetry,\n72\t    InitialRandom,\n73\t    ResetSeed,\n74\t    DisablePortBlocking,\n75\t    SolutionDir,\n76\t    CcAlgo,\n77\t    CcOption,\n78\t    Spinbit,\n79\t    Lossbit,\n80\t    Multipath,\n81\t    DestIf,\n82\t    CipherSuite,\n83\t    InitCnxId,\n84\t    LogFile,\n85\t    LongLog,\n86\t    BinlogDir,\n87\t    QlogDir,\n88\t    MtuMax,\n89\t    Sni,\n90\t    Alpn,\n91\t    RootTrustFile,\n92\t    ForceZeroShare,\n93\t    CnxIdLength,\n94\t    NoDisk,\n95\t    IdleTimeout,\n96\t    LargeClientHello,\n97\t    TicketFileName,\n98\t    TokenFileName,\n99\t    SocketBufferSize,\n100\t    PerformanceLog,\n101\t    PreemptiveRepeat,\n102\t    VersionUpgrade,\n103\t    NoGso,\n104\t    BdpFrame,\n105\t    CwinMax,\n106\t    SslKeyLog,\n107\t    AddressDiscovery,\n108\t    EchServer,\n109\t    EchClient,\n110\t    EchInit,\n111\t    FlowControlMax,\n112\t    PreferredV4,\n113\t    PreferredV6,\n114\t    Help,\n115\t}\n116\t\n117\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n118\t// Option table (mirrors C static option_table[]).\n119\t\n120\tstruct OptionEntry {\n121\t    id: OptionId,\n122\t    letter: char,\n123\t    name: &'static str,\n124\t    nb_params: usize,\n125\t    param_sample: &'static str,\n126\t    help: &'static str,\n127\t}\n128\t\n129\tstatic OPTION_TABLE: &[OptionEntry] = &[\n130\t    OptionEntry {\n131\t        id: OptionId::Cert,\n132\t        letter: 'c',\n133\t        name: \"cert\",\n134\t        nb_params: 1,\n135\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n136\t        help: \"cert file\",\n137\t    },\n138\t    OptionEntry {\n139\t        id: OptionId::Key,\n140\t        letter: 'k',\n141\t        name: \"key\",\n142\t        nb_params: 1,\n143\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n144\t        help: \"key file\",\n145\t    },\n146\t    OptionEntry {\n147\t        id: OptionId::ServerPort,\n148\t        letter: 'p',\n149\t        name: \"port\",\n150\t        nb_params: 1,\n151\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n152\t        help: \"server port\",\n153\t    },\n154\t    OptionEntry {\n155\t        id: OptionId::ProposedVersion,\n156\t        letter: 'v',\n157\t        name: \"proposed_version\",\n158\t        nb_params: 1,\n159\t        param_sample: \"\",\n160\t        help: \"Version proposed by client, e.g. -v ff000012\",\n161\t    },\n162\t    OptionEntry {\n163\t        id: OptionId::OutDir,\n164\t        letter: 'o',\n165\t        name: \"outdir\",\n166\t        nb_params: 1,\n167\t        param_sample: \"folder\",\n168\t        help: \"Folder where client writes downloaded files, defaults to current directory.\",\n169\t    },\n170\t    OptionEntry {\n171\t        id: OptionId::WwwDir,\n172\t        letter: 'w',\n173\t        name: \"wwwdir\",\n174\t        nb_params: 1,\n175\t        param_sample: \"folder\",\n176\t        help: \"Folder containing web pages served by server\",\n177\t    },\n178\t    OptionEntry {\n179\t        id: OptionId::MaxConnections,\n180\t        letter: 'x',\n181\t        name: \"max_connections\",\n182\t        nb_params: 1,\n183\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n184\t        help: \"Maximum number of concurrent connections, default 256\",\n185\t    },\n186\t    OptionEntry {\n187\t        id: OptionId::DoRetry,\n188\t        letter: 'r',\n189\t        name: \"do_retry\",\n190\t        nb_params: 0,\n191\t        param_sample: \"\",\n192\t        help: \"Do Retry Request\",\n193\t    },\n194\t    OptionEntry {\n195\t        id: OptionId::InitialRandom,\n196\t        letter: 'R',\n197\t        name: \"initial_random\",\n198\t        nb_params: 1,\n199\t        param_sample: \"option\",\n200\t        help: \"Randomize packet number spaces: none(0), initial(1, default), all(2).\",\n201\t    },\n202\t    OptionEntry {\n203\t        id: OptionId::ResetSeed,\n204\t        letter: 's',\n205\t        name: \"reset_seed\",\n206\t        nb_params: 1,\n207\t        param_sample: \"<32 hex chars>\",\n208\t        help: \"Reset seed\",\n209\t    },\n210\t    OptionEntry {\n211\t        id: OptionId::DisablePortBlocking,\n212\t        letter: 'X',\n213\t        name: \"disable_block\",\n214\t        nb_params: 0,\n215\t        param_sample: \"\",\n216\t        help: \"Disable the check for blocked ports\",\n217\t    },\n218\t    OptionEntry {\n219\t        id: OptionId::SolutionDir,\n220\t        letter: 'S',\n221\t        name: \"solution_dir\",\n222\t        nb_params: 1,\n223\t        param_sample: \"folder\",\n224\t        help: \"Set the path to the source files to find the default files\",\n225\t    },\n226\t    OptionEntry {\n227\t        id: OptionId::CcAlgo,\n228\t        letter: 'G',\n229\t        name: \"cc_algo\",\n230\t        nb_params: 1,\n231\t        param_sample: \"cc_algorithm\",\n232\t        help: \"Use the specified congestion control algorithm. Defaults to bbr.\",\n233\t    },\n234\t    OptionEntry {\n235\t        id: OptionId::CcOption,\n236\t        letter: 'H',\n237\t        name: \"cco\",\n238\t        nb_params: 1,\n239\t        param_sample: \"option\",\n240\t        help: \"Set option string if required by congestion control algorithm.\",\n241\t    },\n242\t    OptionEntry {\n243\t        id: OptionId::Spinbit,\n244\t        letter: 'P',\n245\t        name: \"spinbit\",\n246\t        nb_params: 1,\n247\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n248\t        help: \"Set the default spinbit policy\",\n249\t    },\n250\t    OptionEntry {\n251\t        id: OptionId::Lossbit,\n252\t        letter: 'O',\n253\t        name: \"lossbit\",\n254\t        nb_params: 1,\n255\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n256\t        help: \"Set the default lossbit policy\",\n257\t    },\n258\t    OptionEntry {\n259\t        id: OptionId::Multipath,\n260\t        letter: 'M',\n261\t        name: \"multipath\",\n262\t        nb_params: 0,\n263\t        param_sample: \"\",\n264\t        help: \"Enable QUIC multipath extension\",\n265\t    },\n266\t    OptionEntry {\n267\t        id: OptionId::DestIf,\n268\t        letter: 'e',\n269\t        name: \"dest_if\",\n270\t        nb_params: 1,\n271\t        param_sample: \"if\",\n272\t        help: \"Send on interface (default: -1)\",\n273\t    },\n274\t    OptionEntry {\n275\t        id: OptionId::CipherSuite,\n276\t        letter: 'C',\n277\t        name: \"cipher_suite\",\n278\t        nb_params: 1,\n279\t        param_sample: \"cipher_suite_id\",\n280\t        help: \"specify cipher suite (e.g. -C 20 = chacha20)\",\n281\t    },\n282\t    OptionEntry {\n283\t        id: OptionId::InitCnxId,\n284\t        letter: 'i',\n285\t        name: \"cnxid_params\",\n286\t        nb_params: 1,\n287\t        param_sample: \"per-text-lb-spec\",\n288\t        help: \"See documentation for LB compatible CID configuration\",\n289\t    },\n290\t    OptionEntry {\n291\t        id: OptionId::LogFile,\n292\t        letter: 'l',\n293\t        name: \"text_log\",\n294\t        nb_params: 1,\n295\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n296\t        help: \"Log file, Log to stdout if file = \\\"-\\\". No text logging if absent.\",\n297\t    },\n298\t    OptionEntry {\n299\t        id: OptionId::LongLog,\n300\t        letter: 'L',\n301\t        name: \"long_log\",\n302\t        nb_params: 0,\n303\t        param_sample: \"\",\n304\t        help: \"Log all packets. If absent, log stops after 100 packets.\",\n305\t    },\n306\t    OptionEntry {\n307\t        id: OptionId::BinlogDir,\n308\t        letter: 'b',\n309\t        name: \"binlog_dir\",\n310\t        nb_params: 1,\n311\t        param_sample: \"folder\",\n312\t        help: \"Binary logging to this directory. No binary logging if absent.\",\n313\t    },\n314\t    OptionEntry {\n315\t        id: OptionId::QlogDir,\n316\t        letter: 'q',\n317\t        name: \"qlog_dir\",\n318\t        nb_params: 1,\n319\t        param_sample: \"folder\",\n320\t        help: \"Qlog logging to this directory.\",\n321\t    },\n322\t    OptionEntry {\n323\t        id: OptionId::MtuMax,\n324\t        letter: 'm',\n325\t        name: \"mtu_max\",\n326\t        nb_params: 1,\n327\t        param_sample: \"mtu_max\",\n328\t        help: \"Largest mtu value that can be tried for discovery.\",\n329\t    },\n330\t    OptionEntry {\n331\t        id: OptionId::Sni,\n332\t        letter: 'n',\n333\t        name: \"sni\",\n334\t        nb_params: 1,\n335\t        param_sample: \"sni\",\n336\t        help: \"sni (default: server name)\",\n337\t    },\n338\t    OptionEntry {\n339\t        id: OptionId::Alpn,\n340\t        letter: 'a',\n341\t        name: \"alpn\",\n342\t        nb_params: 1,\n343\t        param_sample: \"alpn\",\n344\t        help: \"alpn (default function of version)\",\n345\t    },\n346\t    OptionEntry {\n347\t        id: OptionId::RootTrustFile,\n348\t        letter: 't',\n349\t        name: \"root_trust_file\",\n350\t        nb_params: 1,\n351\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n352\t        help: \"root trust file\",\n353\t    },\n354\t    OptionEntry {\n355\t        id: OptionId::ForceZeroShare,\n356\t        letter: 'z',\n357\t        name: \"force_zero_share\",\n358\t        nb_params: 0,\n359\t        param_sample: \"\",\n360\t        help: \"Set TLS zero share behavior on client, to force HRR\",\n361\t    },\n362\t    OptionEntry {\n363\t        id: OptionId::CnxIdLength,\n364\t        letter: 'I',\n365\t        name: \"cnxid_length\",\n366\t        nb_params: 1,\n367\t        param_sample: \"length\",\n368\t        help: \"Length of CNX_ID used by the client, default=8\",\n369\t    },\n370\t    OptionEntry {\n371\t        id: OptionId::IdleTimeout,\n372\t        letter: 'd',\n373\t        name: \"idle_timeout\",\n374\t        nb_params: 1,\n375\t        param_sample: \"ms\",\n376\t        help: \"Duration of idle timeout in milliseconds (Default 30,000ms)\",\n377\t    },\n378\t    OptionEntry {\n379\t        id: OptionId::NoDisk,\n380\t        letter: 'D',\n381\t        name: \"no_disk\",\n382\t        nb_params: 0,\n383\t        param_sample: \"\",\n384\t        help: \"no disk: do not save received files on disk\",\n385\t    },\n386\t    OptionEntry {\n387\t        id: OptionId::LargeClientHello,\n388\t        letter: 'Q',\n389\t        name: \"large_client_hello\",\n390\t        nb_params: 0,\n391\t        param_sample: \"\",\n392\t        help: \"send a large client hello in order to test post quantum readiness\",\n393\t    },\n394\t    OptionEntry {\n395\t        id: OptionId::TicketFileName,\n396\t        letter: 'T',\n397\t        name: \"ticket_file\",\n398\t        nb_params: 1,\n399\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n400\t        help: \"File storing the session tickets\",\n401\t    },\n402\t    OptionEntry {\n403\t        id: OptionId::TokenFileName,\n404\t        letter: 'N',\n405\t        name: \"token_file\",\n406\t        nb_params: 1,\n407\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n408\t        help: \"File storing the new tokens\",\n409\t    },\n410\t    OptionEntry {\n411\t        id: OptionId::SocketBufferSize,\n412\t        letter: 'B',\n413\t        name: \"so_buf_size\",\n414\t        nb_params: 1,\n415\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n416\t        help: \"Set buffer size with SO_SNDBUF SO_RCVBUF\",\n417\t    },\n418\t    OptionEntry {\n419\t        id: OptionId::PerformanceLog,\n420\t        letter: 'F',\n421\t        name: \"log_file_name\",\n422\t        nb_params: 1,\n423\t        param_sample: \"file\",\n424\t        help: \"Append performance reports to performance log\",\n425\t    },\n426\t    OptionEntry {\n427\t        id: OptionId::PreemptiveRepeat,\n428\t        letter: 'V',\n429\t        name: \"preemptive_repeat\",\n430\t        nb_params: 0,\n431\t        param_sample: \"\",\n432\t        help: \"enable preemptive repeat\",\n433\t    },\n434\t    OptionEntry {\n435\t        id: OptionId::VersionUpgrade,\n436\t        letter: 'U',\n437\t        name: \"version_upgrade\",\n438\t        nb_params: 1,\n439\t        param_sample: \"\",\n440\t        help: \"Version upgrade if server agrees, e.g. -U 6b3343cf\",\n441\t    },\n442\t    OptionEntry {\n443\t        id: OptionId::NoGso,\n444\t        letter: '0',\n445\t        name: \"no_gso\",\n446\t        nb_params: 0,\n447\t        param_sample: \"\",\n448\t        help: \"Do not use UDP GSO or equivalent\",\n449\t    },\n450\t    OptionEntry {\n451\t        id: OptionId::BdpFrame,\n452\t        letter: 'j',\n453\t        name: \"bdp\",\n454\t        nb_params: 1,\n455\t        param_sample: \"number\",\n456\t        help: \"use bdp extension frame(1) or don't (0). Default=0\",\n457\t    },\n458\t    OptionEntry {\n459\t        id: OptionId::CwinMax,\n460\t        letter: 'W',\n461\t        name: \"cwin_max\",\n462\t        nb_params: 1,\n463\t        param_sample: \"bytes\",\n464\t        help: \"Max value for CWIN. Default=UINT64_MAX\",\n465\t    },\n466\t    OptionEntry {\n467\t        id: OptionId::SslKeyLog,\n468\t        letter: '8',\n469\t        name: \"sslkeylog\",\n470\t        nb_params: 0,\n471\t        param_sample: \"\",\n472\t        help: \"Enable SSLKEYLOG\",\n473\t    },\n474\t    OptionEntry {\n475\t        id: OptionId::AddressDiscovery,\n476\t        letter: 'J',\n477\t        name: \"addr_disc\",\n478\t        nb_params: 1,\n479\t        param_sample: \"mode\",\n480\t        help: \"provider (0), receiver (1) or both (2).\",\n481\t    },\n482\t    OptionEntry {\n483\t        id: OptionId::EchServer,\n484\t        letter: 'E',\n485\t        name: \"ech_s\",\n486\t        nb_params: 2,\n487\t        param_sample: \"key config\",\n488\t        help: \"ECH private key file, config file. Default= no ECH on server.\",\n489\t    },\n490\t    OptionEntry {\n491\t        id: OptionId::EchInit,\n492\t        letter: 'y',\n493\t        name: \"ech_init\",\n494\t        nb_params: 1,\n495\t        param_sample: \"public_name\",\n496\t        help: \"Create an ECH configuration before applying the `ech_s` parameter.\",\n497\t    },\n498\t    OptionEntry {\n499\t        id: OptionId::EchClient,\n500\t        letter: 'K',\n501\t        name: \"ech_c\",\n502\t        nb_params: 1,\n503\t        param_sample: \"base64\",\n504\t        help: \"ECH configuration for the client connection, base64 encoded.\",\n505\t    },\n506\t    OptionEntry {\n507\t        id: OptionId::FlowControlMax,\n508\t        letter: 'Z',\n509\t        name: \"flow_control_max\",\n510\t        nb_params: 1,\n511\t        param_sample: \"bytes\",\n512\t        help: \"Set the flow control's initial max data.\",\n513\t    },\n514\t    OptionEntry {\n515\t        id: OptionId::PreferredV4,\n516\t        letter: '4',\n517\t        name: \"preferred_v4\",\n518\t        nb_params: 1,\n519\t        param_sample: \"ip[:port]\",\n520\t        help: \"Preferred address for v4 connections.\",\n521\t    },\n522\t    OptionEntry {\n523\t        id: OptionId::PreferredV6,\n524\t        letter: '6',\n525\t        name: \"preferred_v6\",\n526\t        nb_params: 1,\n527\t        param_sample: \"ipv6[:port]\",\n528\t        help: \"Preferred address for v6 connections.\",\n529\t    },\n530\t    OptionEntry {\n531\t        id: OptionId::Help,\n532\t        letter: 'h',\n533\t        name: \"help\",\n534\t        nb_params: 0,\n535\t        param_sample: \"\",\n536\t        help: \"This help message\",\n537\t    },\n538\t];\n539\t\n540\tfn parse_hex_version(s: &str) -> u32 {\n541\t    u32::from_str_radix(s, 16).unwrap_or(0)\n542\t}\n543\t\n544\tfn base64_decode(s: &str) -> Result<Vec<u8>, Error> {\n545\t    let mut table = [0xFFu8; 256];\n546\t    for (i, &c) in b\"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/\"\n547\t        .iter()\n548\t        .enumerate()\n549\t    {\n550\t        table[c as usize] = i as u8;\n551\t    }\n552\t    let bytes: Vec<u8> = s.bytes().filter(|&c| c != b'=').collect();\n553\t    let mut out = Vec::new();\n554\t    for chunk in bytes.chunks(4) {\n555\t        let mut v = [0u8; 4];\n556\t        let n = chunk.len();\n557\t        for (i, &b) in chunk.iter().enumerate() {\n558\t            let x = table[b as usize];\n559\t            if x == 0xFF {\n560\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n561\t            }\n562\t            v[i] = x;\n563\t        }\n564\t        out.push((v[0] << 2) | (v[1] >> 4));\n565\t        if n >= 3 {\n566\t            out.push((v[1] << 4) | (v[2] >> 2));\n567\t        }\n568\t        if n == 4 {\n569\t            out.push((v[2] << 6) | v[3]);\n570\t        }\n571\t    }\n572\t    Ok(out)\n573\t}\n574\t\n575\tfn option_entry(id: OptionId) -> Option<&'static OptionEntry> {\n576\t    OPTION_TABLE.iter().find(|e| e.id == id)\n577\t}\n578\t\n579\tfn option_entry_by_letter(letter: char) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> {\n580\t    OPTION_TABLE\n581\t        .iter()\n582\t        .enumerate()\n583\t        .find(|(_, e)| e.letter == letter)\n584\t}\n585\t\n586\tfn option_entry_by_name(name: &str) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> {\n587\t    OPTION_TABLE\n588\t        .iter()\n589\t        .enumerate()\n590\t        .find(|(_, e)| e.name == name)\n591\t}\n592\t\n593\tfn apply_option(config: &mut Config, entry: &OptionEntry, params: &[&str]) -> Result<(), Error> {\n594\t    let p0 = params.first().copied();\n595\t    let p1 = params.get(1).copied();\n596\t    match entry.id {\n597\t        OptionId::Cert => {\n598\t            config.server_cert_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n599\t        }\n600\t        OptionId::Key => {\n601\t            config.server_key_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n602\t        }\n603\t        OptionId::ServerPort => {\n604\t            config.set_port(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?)?;\n605\t        }\n606\t        OptionId::ProposedVersion => {\n607\t            let v = parse_hex_version(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?);\n608\t            if v == 0 {\n609\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n610\t            }\n611\t            config.proposed_version = v;\n612\t        }\n613\t        OptionId::OutDir => {\n614\t            config.out_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n615\t        }\n616\t        OptionId::WwwDir => {\n617\t            config.www_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n618\t        }\n619\t        OptionId::MaxConnections => {\n620\t            let v: i32 = p0\n621\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n622\t                .parse()\n623\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n624\t            if v <= 0 {\n625\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n626\t            }\n627\t            config.nb_connections = v as u32;\n628\t        }\n629\t        OptionId::DoRetry => {\n630\t            config.do_retry = true;\n631\t        }\n632\t        OptionId::InitialRandom => {\n633\t            let v: i32 = p0\n634\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n635\t                .parse()\n636\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n637\t            if !(0..=2).contains(&v) {\n638\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n639\t            }\n640\t            config.initial_random = v as u32;\n641\t        }\n642\t        OptionId::ResetSeed => {\n643\t            config.has_reset_seed = true;\n644\t            let n =\n645\t                crate::utils::parse_hexa(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?, &mut config.reset_seed);\n646\t            if n != config.reset_seed.len() {\n647\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n648\t            }\n649\t        }\n650\t        OptionId::DisablePortBlocking => {\n651\t            config.disable_port_blocking = true;\n652\t        }\n653\t        OptionId::SslKeyLog => {\n654\t            config.enable_sslkeylog = true;\n655\t        }\n656\t        OptionId::SolutionDir => {\n657\t            config.solution_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n658\t        }\n659\t        OptionId::CcAlgo => {\n660\t            config.cc_algo_id = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n661\t        }\n662\t        OptionId::CcOption => {\n663\t            config.cc_algo_option_string = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n664\t        }\n665\t        OptionId::Spinbit => {\n666\t            let v: i32 = p0\n667\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n668\t                .parse()\n669\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n670\t            config.spinbit_policy = match v {\n671\t                0 => SpinbitVersion::Basic,\n672\t                1 => SpinbitVersion::Random,\n673\t                2 => SpinbitVersion::Null,\n674\t                3 => SpinbitVersion::On,\n675\t                _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n676\t            };\n677\t        }\n678\t        OptionId::Lossbit => {\n679\t            let v: i32 = p0\n680\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n681\t                .parse()\n682\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n683\t            config.lossbit_policy = match v {\n684\t                0 => LossbitVersion::None,\n685\t                1 => LossbitVersion::SendOnly,\n686\t                2 => LossbitVersion::SendReceive,\n687\t                _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n688\t            };\n689\t        }\n690\t        OptionId::Multipath => {\n691\t            config.multipath_option = 1;\n692\t        }\n693\t        OptionId::DestIf => {\n694\t            config.dest_if = p0\n695\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n696\t                .parse()\n697\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n698\t        }\n699\t        OptionId::CipherSuite => {\n700\t            config.cipher_suite_id = p0\n701\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n702\t                .parse()\n703\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n704\t        }\n705\t        OptionId::InitCnxId => {\n706\t            config.connection_id_cbdata = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n707\t        }\n708\t        OptionId::LogFile => {\n709\t            config.log_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n710\t        }\n711\t        OptionId::LongLog => {\n712\t            config.use_long_log = true;\n713\t        }\n714\t        OptionId::BinlogDir => {\n715\t            config.bin_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n716\t        }\n717\t        OptionId::QlogDir => {\n718\t            config.qlog_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n719\t        }\n720\t        OptionId::MtuMax => {\n721\t            let v: i32 = p0\n722\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n723\t                .parse()\n724\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n725\t            if v <= 0 || v > crate::internal::MAX_PACKET_SIZE as i32 {\n726\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n727\t            }\n728\t            config.mtu_max = v;\n729\t        }\n730\t        OptionId::Sni => {\n731\t            config.sni = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n732\t        }\n733\t        OptionId::Alpn => {\n734\t            config.alpn = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n735\t        }\n736\t        OptionId::RootTrustFile => {\n737\t            config.root_trust_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n738\t        }\n739\t        OptionId::ForceZeroShare => {\n740\t            config.force_zero_share = true;\n741\t        }\n742\t        OptionId::CnxIdLength => {\n743\t            let v: i32 = p0\n744\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n745\t                .parse()\n746\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n747\t            if v < 0 || v > crate::CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE as i32 {\n748\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n749\t            }\n750\t            config.connection_id_length = v;\n751\t        }\n752\t        OptionId::IdleTimeout => {\n753\t            let v: i32 = p0\n754\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n755\t                .parse()\n756\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n757\t            if v < 0 {\n758\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n759\t            }\n760\t            config.idle_timeout = v;\n761\t        }\n762\t        OptionId::NoDisk => {\n763\t            config.no_disk = true;\n764\t        }\n765\t        OptionId::LargeClientHello => {\n766\t            config.large_client_hello = true;\n767\t        }\n768\t        OptionId::TicketFileName => {\n769\t            config.ticket_file_name = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n770\t        }\n771\t        OptionId::TokenFileName => {\n772\t            config.token_file_name = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n773\t        }\n774\t        OptionId::SocketBufferSize => {\n775\t            let v: i32 = p0\n776\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n777\t                .parse()\n778\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n779\t            if v < 0 {\n780\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n781\t            }\n782\t            config.socket_buffer_size = v;\n783\t        }\n784\t        OptionId::PerformanceLog => {\n785\t            config.performance_log = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n786\t        }\n787\t        OptionId::PreemptiveRepeat => {\n788\t            config.do_preemptive_repeat = true;\n789\t        }\n790\t        OptionId::VersionUpgrade => {\n791\t            let v = parse_hex_version(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?);\n792\t            if v == 0 {\n793\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n794\t            }\n795\t            config.desired_version = v;\n796\t        }\n797\t        OptionId::NoGso => {\n798\t            config.do_not_use_gso = true;\n799\t        }\n800\t        OptionId::BdpFrame => {\n801\t            let v: i32 = p0\n802\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n803\t                .parse()\n804\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n805\t            if !(0..=1).contains(&v) {\n806\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n807\t            }\n808\t            config.bdp_frame_option = v;\n809\t        }\n810\t        OptionId::CwinMax => {\n811\t            let v: i64 = p0\n812\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n813\t                .parse()\n814\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n815\t            if v < 0 {\n816\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n817\t            }\n818\t            config.cwin_max = if v == 0 { u64::MAX } else { v as u64 };\n819\t        }\n820\t        OptionId::AddressDiscovery => {\n821\t            let v: i32 = p0\n822\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n823\t                .parse()\n824\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n825\t            if !(0..=2).contains(&v) {\n826\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n827\t            }\n828\t            config.address_discovery_mode = v + 1;\n829\t        }\n830\t        OptionId::EchServer => {\n831\t            config.ech_key_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n832\t            if let Some(s) = p1 {\n833\t                config.ech_config_file = Some(s.to_string());\n834\t            }\n835\t        }\n836\t        OptionId::EchInit => {\n837\t            config.ech_public_name = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n838\t        }\n839\t        OptionId::EchClient => {\n840\t            let s = p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n841\t            if s == \"-\" {\n842\t                config.ech_target = None;\n843\t            } else {\n844\t                config.ech_target = Some(base64_decode(s).map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?);\n845\t            }\n846\t        }\n847\t        OptionId::FlowControlMax => {\n848\t            let v: i64 = p0\n849\t                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n850\t                .parse()\n851\t                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n852\t            if v < 0 {\n853\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n854\t            }\n855\t            config.flow_control_max = v as u64;\n856\t        }\n857\t        OptionId::PreferredV4 => {\n858\t            config.preferred_address_v4 = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n859\t        }\n860\t        OptionId::PreferredV6 => {\n861\t            config.preferred_address_v6 = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n862\t        }\n863\t        OptionId::Help => {\n864\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n865\t        }\n866\t    }\n867\t    Ok(())\n868\t}\n869\t\n870\tfn collect_params<'a>(\n871\t    entry: &OptionEntry,\n872\t    p_optind: &mut usize,\n873\t    argv: &[&'a str],\n874\t    optarg: Option<&'a str>,\n875\t) -> Result<Vec<&'a str>, Error> {\n876\t    let mut params = Vec::new();\n877\t    if entry.nb_params > 0 {\n878\t        params.push(optarg.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?);\n879\t        let mut nb = 1;\n880\t        while nb < entry.nb_params {\n881\t            if *p_optind >= argv.len() {\n882\t                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n883\t            }\n884\t            params.push(argv[*p_optind]);\n885\t            *p_optind += 1;\n886\t            nb += 1;\n887\t        }\n888\t    }\n889\t    Ok(params)\n890\t}\n891\t\n892\tfn parse_option_string(opt_string: &str) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> {\n893\t    if opt_string.starts_with(\"--\") && opt_string.len() > 2 {\n894\t        option_entry_by_name(&opt_string[2..])\n895\t    } else if opt_string.starts_with('-') && opt_string.len() == 2 {\n896\t        opt_string.chars().nth(1).and_then(option_entry_by_letter)\n897\t    } else {\n898\t        None\n899\t    }\n900\t}\n901\t\n902\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n903\t// Configuration struct.\n904\t\n905\t/// Configuration bag for a QUIC context, populated from CLI flags\n906\t/// (via [`Config::command_line`]) or directly (via\n907\t/// [`Config::set_option`]) and consumed by\n908\t/// [`Config::create_and_configure`].\n909\t///\n910\t/// Mirrors the C `picoquic_quic_config_t` field-for-field;\n911\t/// `repr(C)` is dropped because the struct never crosses an\n912\t/// external boundary.  See the module-level docs for the\n913\t/// pointer-shape rationale.\n914\t///\n915\t/// `Default` produces the documented C defaults:\n916\t/// `nb_connections = 256`, `connection_id_length = -1`, `cwin_max =\n917\t/// u64::MAX`, idle timeout from `MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX`, etc.  This\n918\t/// folds the C `picoquic_config_init` step into the constructor —\n919\t/// the C `config_clear` (which `free`s every owned string) collapses\n920\t/// to `Drop`, and resetting a config to defaults is just\n921\t/// `*config = Config::default()`.\n922\t#[derive(Debug)]\n923\tpub struct Config {\n924\t    pub nb_connections: u32,\n925\t    pub solution_dir: Option<String>,\n926\t    pub server_cert_file: Option<String>,\n927\t    pub server_key_file: Option<String>,\n928\t    pub log_file: Option<String>,\n929\t    pub bin_dir: Option<String>,\n930\t    pub qlog_dir: Option<String>,\n931\t    pub performance_log: Option<String>,\n932\t    pub server_port: u16,\n933\t    pub local_port: u16,\n934\t    /// Whether the public port is shared with sibling threads\n935\t    /// (`SO_REUSEPORT`).  C: `int is_port_shared`, used as a\n936\t    /// Boolean flag.\n937\t    pub is_port_shared: bool,\n938\t    pub nb_threads: i32,\n939\t    pub dest_if: i32,\n940\t    pub mtu_max: i32,\n941\t    /// `-1` is the C \"unset\" sentinel applied by [`Self::init`];\n942\t    /// values `>= 0` set the connection-ID length explicitly.  Kept\n943\t    /// as `i32` rather than `Option<u8>` for source-level parity\n944\t    /// with the C body.\n945\t    pub connection_id_length: i32,\n946\t    pub idle_timeout: i32,\n947\t    pub socket_buffer_size: i32,\n948\t    pub cc_algo_id: Option<String>,\n949\t    pub cc_algo_option_string: Option<String>,\n950\t    pub connection_id_cbdata: Option<String>,\n951\t    pub spinbit_policy: SpinbitVersion,\n952\t    pub lossbit_policy: LossbitVersion,\n953\t    pub multipath_option: i32,\n954\t    pub multipath_alt_config: Option<String>,\n955\t    pub bdp_frame_option: i32,\n956\t    pub cwin_max: u64,\n957\t    pub address_discovery_mode: i32,\n958\t\n959\t    // Common flags.\n960\t    pub initial_random: u32,\n961\t    pub use_long_log: bool,\n962\t    pub do_preemptive_repeat: bool,\n963\t    pub do_not_use_gso: bool,\n964\t    pub disable_port_blocking: bool,\n965\t    /// Originally bitfield-gated by `#ifndef\n966\t    /// WITHOUT_SSLKEYLOG`; v1 follows the canonical build\n967\t    /// (always defined), so the field is unconditional here.\n968\t    pub enable_sslkeylog: bool,\n969\t\n970\t    // Server only.\n971\t    pub www_dir: Option<String>,\n972\t    pub reset_seed: [u8; 16],\n973\t    /// Borrowed in C (`config_clear` does not free it); owned\n974\t    /// `Vec<u8>` here for safety.  The C\n975\t    /// `ticket_encryption_key_length` field is dropped — its value\n976\t    /// is always `ticket_encryption_key.as_ref().map_or(0, Vec::len)`.\n977\t    pub ticket_encryption_key: Option<Vec<u8>>,\n978\t\n979\t    // Server flags.\n980\t    pub do_retry: bool,\n981\t    pub has_reset_seed: bool,\n982\t\n983\t    // Client only.\n984\t    pub ticket_file_name: Option<String>,\n985\t    pub token_file_name: Option<String>,\n986\t    pub sni: Option<String>,\n987\t    pub alpn: Option<String>,\n988\t    pub out_dir: Option<String>,\n989\t    pub root_trust_file: Option<String>,\n990\t    pub cipher_suite_id: i32,\n991\t    pub proposed_version: u32,\n992\t    pub desired_version: u32,\n993\t    pub force_zero_share: bool,\n994\t    pub no_disk: bool,\n995\t    pub large_client_hello: bool,\n996\t\n997\t    // ECH parameters for server.\n998\t    pub ech_key_file: Option<String>,\n999\t    pub ech_config_file: Option<String>,\n1000\t    pub ech_public_name: Option<String>,\n1001\t    /// ECH parameter for the client, base64-decoded.  Owned by\n1002\t    /// the config — `config_clear` frees it in C.  The C\n1003\t    /// `ech_target_len` field is dropped — its value is always\n1004\t    /// `ech_target.as_ref().map_or(0, Vec::len)`.\n1005\t    pub ech_target: Option<Vec<u8>>,\n1006\t\n1007\t    pub flow_control_max: u64,\n1008\t\n1009\t    // Preferred address, encoded as strings.\n1010\t    pub preferred_address_v4: Option<String>,\n1011\t    pub preferred_address_v6: Option<String>,\n1012\t}\n1013\t\n1014\timpl Default for Config {\n1015\t    /// Build a fresh config with the documented C defaults.  C:\n1016\t    /// `picoquic_config_init` (which the C body invoked after a\n1017\t    /// zero-initialising `memset`).\n1018\t    fn default() -> Self {\n1019\t        Config {\n1020\t            nb_connections: 256,\n1021\t            solution_dir: None,\n1022\t            server_cert_file: None,\n1023\t            server_key_file: None,\n1024\t            log_file: None,\n1025\t            bin_dir: None,\n1026\t            qlog_dir: None,\n1027\t            performance_log: None,\n1028\t            server_port: 0,\n1029\t            local_port: 0,\n1030\t            is_port_shared: false,\n1031\t            nb_threads: 0,\n1032\t            dest_if: 0,\n1033\t            mtu_max: 0,\n1034\t            connection_id_length: -1,\n1035\t            idle_timeout: (MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX.ticks() / 1000) as i32,\n1036\t            socket_buffer_size: 0,\n1037\t            cc_algo_id: None,\n1038\t            cc_algo_option_string: None,\n1039\t            connection_id_cbdata: None,\n1040\t            spinbit_policy: SpinbitVersion::default(),\n1041\t            lossbit_policy: LossbitVersion::default(),\n1042\t            multipath_option: 0,\n1043\t            multipath_alt_config: None,\n1044\t            bdp_frame_option: 0,\n1045\t            cwin_max: u64::MAX,\n1046\t            address_discovery_mode: 0,\n1047\t            initial_random: 3,\n1048\t            use_long_log: false,\n1049\t            do_preemptive_repeat: false,\n1050\t            do_not_use_gso: false,\n1051\t            disable_port_blocking: false,\n1052\t            enable_sslkeylog: false,\n1053\t            www_dir: None,\n1054\t            reset_seed: [0; 16],\n1055\t            ticket_encryption_key: None,\n1056\t            do_retry: false,\n1057\t            has_reset_seed: false,\n1058\t            ticket_file_name: None,\n1059\t            token_file_name: None,\n1060\t            sni: None,\n1061\t            alpn: None,\n1062\t            out_dir: None,\n1063\t            root_trust_file: None,\n1064\t            cipher_suite_id: 0,\n1065\t            proposed_version: 0,\n1066\t            desired_version: 0,\n1067\t            force_zero_share: false,\n1068\t            no_disk: false,\n1069\t            large_client_hello: false,\n1070\t            ech_key_file: None,\n1071\t            ech_config_file: None,\n1072\t            ech_public_name: None,\n1073\t            ech_target: None,\n1074\t            flow_control_max: 0,\n1075\t            preferred_address_v4: None,\n1076\t            preferred_address_v6: None,\n1077\t        }\n1078\t    }\n1079\t}\n1080\t\n1081\timpl Config {\n1082\t    /// Apply one option, selected by `option`, to the config.\n1083\t    /// C: `picoquic_config_set_option`.\n1084\t    ///\n1085\t    /// `value` is optional — flag-style options ([`OptionId::DoRetry`],\n1086\t    /// [`OptionId::LongLog`], …) ignore it; value-style options\n1087\t    /// require it and return `Err` when it is missing or malformed.\n1088\t    ///\n1089\t    /// The C signature returned `int` (`0` ↔ `Ok`, `-1` ↔ `Err`);\n1090\t    /// mapped to `Result<(), Error>`.\n1091\t    pub fn set_option(&mut self, option: OptionId, value: Option<&str>) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1092\t        let entry = option_entry(option).ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n1093\t        let params: &[&str] = match value {\n1094\t            Some(v) => &[v],\n1095\t            None => &[],\n1096\t        };\n1097\t        apply_option(self, entry, params)\n1098\t    }\n1099\t\n1100\t    /// Dispatch one option from a single-character flag (`-x`).\n1101\t    /// C: `picoquic_config_command_line`.\n1102\t    ///\n1103\t    /// `p_optind` advances past any extra arguments consumed beyond\n1104\t    /// the inline `optarg`, mirroring the C in/out parameter so that\n1105\t    /// an outer getopt-style loop stays in sync.\n1106\t    ///\n1107\t    /// `argv` is a borrowed slice of borrowed strings — the C caller\n1108\t    /// (`first` etc.) owns the argument vector for the program\n1109\t    /// lifetime, so a borrow is safe.  The C `int argc` parameter is\n1110\t    /// dropped (implicit in `argv.len()`).\n1111\t    pub fn command_line(\n1112\t        &mut self,\n1113\t        opt: char,\n1114\t        p_optind: &mut usize,\n1115\t        argv: &[&str],\n1116\t        optarg: Option<&str>,\n1117\t    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1118\t        let (_, entry) = option_entry_by_letter(opt).ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n1119\t        let params = collect_params(entry, p_optind, argv, optarg)?;\n1120\t        apply_option(self, entry, &params)\n1121\t    }\n1122\t\n1123\t    /// Like [`Self::command_line`] but accepts both single-character\n1124\t    /// (`-x`) and long-form (`--name`) option strings; the leading\n1125\t    /// dashes are part of `opt_string`, matching the C contract.\n1126\t    /// C: `picoquic_config_command_line_ex`.\n1127\t    pub fn command_line_ex(\n1128\t        &mut self,\n1129\t        opt_string: &str,\n1130\t        p_optind: &mut usize,\n1131\t        argv: &[&str],\n1132\t        optarg: Option<&str>,\n1133\t    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1134\t        let (_, entry) = parse_option_string(opt_string).ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n1135\t        let params = collect_params(entry, p_optind, argv, optarg)?;\n1136\t        apply_option(self, entry, &params)\n1137\t    }\n1138\t\n1139\t    /// Build the getopt-style option string from the dispatch table\n1140\t    /// in `config.c` — one letter per option, with `:` after each\n1141\t    /// option that takes an argument.  C:\n1142\t    /// `picoquic_config_option_letters`.\n1143\t    ///\n1144\t    /// The C signature wrote into a caller-supplied buffer\n1145\t    /// (`option_string`, `string_max`) and reported the populated\n1146\t    /// length via `*string_length`.  The Rust wrapper owns the\n1147\t    /// buffer and returns it directly, so the buffer-too-small\n1148\t    /// failure mode disappears.\n1149\t    pub fn option_letters() -> String {\n1150\t        let mut s = String::new();\n1151\t        for e in OPTION_TABLE {\n1152\t            s.push(e.letter);\n1153\t            if e.nb_params > 0 {\n1154\t                s.push(':');\n1155\t            }\n1156\t        }\n1157\t        s\n1158\t    }\n1159\t\n1160\t    /// Write the option help to a [`core::fmt::Write`] sink.\n1161\t    /// C: `picoquic_config_usage_file`.\n1162\t    ///\n1163\t    /// The C parameter was `FILE*`; the Rust translation accepts\n1164\t    /// any sink (a `String` buffer, the stdout/stderr handles under\n1165\t    /// the `std` feature, or a custom writer) so the function\n1166\t    /// stays `no_std`-friendly.\n1167\t    pub fn write_usage(w: &mut dyn core::fmt::Write) {\n1168\t        let _ = w.write_str(\"Picoquic options:\\n\");\n1169\t        for e in OPTION_TABLE {\n1170\t            let _ = write!(w, \"  -{} {}\", e.letter, e.param_sample);\n1171\t            let pad = 12usize.saturating_sub(e.param_sample.len());\n1172\t            for _ in 0..pad {\n1173\t                let _ = w.write_char(' ');\n1174\t            }\n1175\t            let _ = writeln!(w, \" {}\", e.help);\n1176\t        }\n1177\t    }\n1178\t\n1179\t    /// Print the option help to stderr.  C: `picoquic_config_usage`.\n1180\t    ///\n1181\t    /// Routes through an intermediate `String` buffer then `eprint!`.\n1182\t    pub fn print_usage() {\n1183\t        let mut buf = String::new();\n1184\t        Self::write_usage(&mut buf);\n1185\t        eprint!(\"{}\", buf);\n1186\t    }\n1187\t\n1188\t    /// Parse a port-configuration string into `server_port`,\n1189\t    /// `local_port`, `is_port_shared`, and `nb_threads`.\n1190\t    /// C: `config_set_port` (internal, called from the `-p` option\n1191\t    /// handler in `picoquic/config.c`).\n1192\t    ///\n1193\t    /// Accepted formats:\n1194\t    /// - `\"\"` / `\"0\"` — clear all (port 0, not shared)\n1195\t    /// - `\"4433\"` — server port only\n1196\t    /// - `\"443:4434\"` — server:local\n1197\t    /// - `\"S4433\"` — shared server port\n1198\t    /// - `\"S443:4434*256\"` — shared server:local, 256 threads\n1199\t    /// - `\"4433*7\"` — server port, 7 threads\n1200\t    ///\n1201\t    /// Returns `Err` when any token cannot be parsed or a port value\n1202\t    /// exceeds 65535.\n1203\t    pub fn set_port(&mut self, port_string: &str) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1204\t        let bytes = port_string.as_bytes();\n1205\t        let mut i = 0;\n1206\t        let mut is_port_shared = false;\n1207\t        let mut p1: i32 = 0;\n1208\t        let mut p2: i32 = 0;\n1209\t        let mut nb_threads: i32 = 0;\n1210\t\n1211\t        if i < bytes.len() && bytes[i] == b'S' {\n1212\t            is_port_shared = true;\n1213\t            i += 1;\n1214\t        }\n1215\t        while i < bytes.len() && bytes[i].is_ascii_digit() {\n1216\t            p1 = p1 * 10 + (bytes[i] - b'0') as i32;\n1217\t            i += 1;\n1218\t        }\n1219\t        if i < bytes.len() && bytes[i] == b':' {\n1220\t            i += 1;\n1221\t            while i < bytes.len() && bytes[i].is_ascii_digit() {\n1222\t                p2 = p2 * 10 + (bytes[i] - b'0') as i32;\n1223\t                i += 1;\n1224\t            }\n1225\t        }\n1226\t        if i < bytes.len() && bytes[i] == b'*' {\n1227\t            i += 1;\n1228\t            while i < bytes.len() && bytes[i].is_ascii_digit() {\n1229\t                nb_threads = nb_threads * 10 + (bytes[i] - b'0') as i32;\n1230\t                i += 1;\n1231\t            }\n1232\t        }\n1233\t        if i != bytes.len() || !(0..=65535).contains(&p1) || !(0..=65535).contains(&p2) {\n1234\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n1235\t        }\n1236\t        self.server_port = p1 as u16;\n1237\t        self.local_port = p2 as u16;\n1238\t        self.is_port_shared = is_port_shared;\n1239\t        self.nb_threads = nb_threads;\n1240\t        Ok(())\n1241\t    }\n1242\t\n1243\t    /// Build a fully-configured QUIC context from this config plus\n1244\t    /// an application-supplied callback.  C:\n1245\t    /// `picoquic_create_and_configure`.\n1246\t    ///\n1247\t    /// Returns `None` when context creation fails (the C side\n1248\t    /// returned `NULL`).\n1249\t    ///\n1250\t    /// Pointer-shape choices, derived from the C signature and the\n1251\t    /// body in `config.c`:\n1252\t    ///\n1253\t    /// * `picoquic_quic_config_t* config` is consumed-borrowed\n1254\t    ///   (`&mut self`): the body reads every field and may set up\n1255\t    ///   downstream owned state, but it does not free the struct\n1256\t    ///   itself — ownership stays with the caller.\n1257\t    /// * `default_callback_fn` + `default_callback_ctx` collapse to\n1258\t    ///   one `Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>` per the\n1259\t    ///   function-pointers-map-to-traits rule, with the `void*`\n1260\t    ///   context folded into the trait implementor's state.  `None`\n1261\t    ///   matches the C \"no default callback\" case where the function\n1262\t    ///   pointer was `NULL`.\n1263\t    /// * `p_simulated_time: *mut u64` carries simulated wall time for\n1264\t    ///   tests; the C QUIC context retains the pointer across calls,\n1265\t    ///   so an `&mut u64` borrow expresses the contract directly.\n1266\t    ///   Phase 3 may revisit (e.g. with a clock trait) once the QUIC\n1267\t    ///   context type is real.\n1268\t    pub fn create_and_configure(\n1269\t        &mut self,\n1270\t        default_callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n1271\t        current_time: Instant,\n1272\t        _p_simulated_time: Option<&mut u64>,\n1273\t    ) -> Option<Box<Quic>> {\n1274\t        let reset_seed = if self.has_reset_seed {\n1275\t            self.reset_seed\n1276\t        } else {\n1277\t            [0u8; 16]\n1278\t        };\n1279\t\n1280\t        let mut quic = Quic::new(\n1281\t            self.nb_connections,\n1282\t            self.server_cert_file.as_deref(),\n1283\t            self.server_key_file.as_deref(),\n1284\t            self.root_trust_file.as_deref(),\n1285\t            self.alpn.as_deref(),\n1286\t            default_callback,\n1287\t            None,\n1288\t            reset_seed,\n1289\t            current_time,\n1290\t            self.ticket_file_name.as_deref(),\n1291\t            self.ticket_encryption_key.as_deref(),\n1292\t        )?;\n1293\t\n1294\t        if self.do_retry {\n1295\t            quic.set_cookie_mode(1);\n1296\t        } else {\n1297\t            quic.set_cookie_mode(2);\n1298\t        }\n1299\t\n1300\t        if let Some(ref cc_id) = self.cc_algo_id {\n1301\t            let _ = quic.set_default_congestion_algorithm_by_name(cc_id);\n1302\t        }\n1303\t\n1304\t        let _ = quic.set_default_spinbit_policy(self.spinbit_policy);\n1305\t        quic.set_default_lossbit_policy(self.lossbit_policy);\n1306\t        quic.set_default_multipath_option(self.multipath_option);\n1307\t        quic.set_default_idle_timeout(crate::Duration::from_ticks(self.idle_timeout as u64 * 1000));\n1308\t        quic.set_cwin_max(self.cwin_max);\n1309\t        quic.set_default_address_discovery_mode(self.address_discovery_mode);\n1310\t\n1311\t        if let Some(ref token_file) = self.token_file_name {\n1312\t            let _ = quic.load_retry_tokens(token_file);\n1313\t        }\n1314\t\n1315\t        if self.force_zero_share {\n1316\t            quic.client_zero_share = true;\n1317\t        }\n1318\t\n1319\t        if self.mtu_max > 0 {\n1320\t            quic.set_mtu_max(self.mtu_max as u32);\n1321\t        }\n1322\t\n1323\t        if self.connection_id_length != -1 {\n1324\t            let _ = quic.set_default_connection_id_length(self.connection_id_length as u8);\n1325\t        }\n1326\t\n1327\t        quic.set_padding_policy(39, 128);\n1328\t\n1329\t        if let Some(ref bin_dir) = self.bin_dir {\n1330\t            let _ = quic.set_binlog(Some(bin_dir.as_str()));\n1331\t        }\n1332\t\n1333\t        if let Some(ref qlog_dir) = self.qlog_dir {\n1334\t            let _ = quic.set_qlog(qlog_dir.as_str());\n1335\t        }\n1336\t\n1337\t        if let Some(ref log_file) = self.log_file {\n1338\t            let _ = quic.set_textlog(Some(log_file.as_str()));\n1339\t        }\n1340\t\n1341\t        quic.set_log_level(if self.use_long_log { 1 } else { 0 });\n1342\t        quic.set_preemptive_repeat_policy(self.do_preemptive_repeat);\n1343\t        quic.set_port_blocking_disabled(self.disable_port_blocking);\n1344\t        quic.set_sslkeylog_enabled(self.enable_sslkeylog);\n1345\t\n1346\t        if self.initial_random <= 2 {\n1347\t            quic.set_random_initial(self.initial_random as i32);\n1348\t        }\n1349\t\n1350\t        if self.cipher_suite_id != 0 {\n1351\t            let iana_code = match self.cipher_suite_id {\n1352\t                20 => crate::CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256,\n1353\t                128 => crate::AES_128_GCM_SHA256,\n1354\t                256 => crate::AES_256_GCM_SHA384,\n1355\t                v => v as u16,\n1356\t            };\n1357\t            let _ = quic.set_cipher_suite(iana_code);\n1358\t        }\n1359\t\n1360\t        if self.do_retry {\n1361\t            quic.set_cookie_mode(1);\n1362\t        } else {\n1363\t            quic.set_cookie_mode(2);\n1364\t        }\n1365\t\n1366\t        quic.set_default_bdp_frame_option(self.bdp_frame_option != 0);\n1367\t\n1368\t        let mut failed = false;\n1369\t\n1370\t        if let Some(ref public_name) = self.ech_public_name {\n1371\t            if self.ech_key_file.is_none() || self.ech_config_file.is_none() {\n1372\t                // key file or config file not specified — cannot create ECH config\n1373\t            } else {\n1374\t                let key_file = self.ech_key_file.as_deref().unwrap();\n1375\t                let cfg_file = self.ech_config_file.as_deref().unwrap();\n1376\t                if crate::ech_create_config_file(public_name, key_file, cfg_file).is_err() {\n1377\t                    failed = true;\n1378\t                }\n1379\t            }\n1380\t        }\n1381\t\n1382\t        if !failed\n1383\t            && (self.ech_key_file.is_some() || self.ech_target.is_some())\n1384\t            && quic\n1385\t                .ech_configure(\n1386\t                    self.ech_key_file.as_deref(),\n1387\t                    self.ech_config_file.as_deref(),\n1388\t                )\n1389\t                .is_err()\n1390\t        {\n1391\t            failed = true;\n1392\t        }\n1393\t\n1394\t        if !failed && self.flow_control_max > 0 {\n1395\t            quic.set_max_data_control(self.flow_control_max);\n1396\t        }\n1397\t\n1398\t        if failed { None } else { Some(quic) }\n1399\t    }\n1400\t}\n1401\t\n1402\t#[cfg(test)]\n1403\tmod test {}\n1404\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"589969e0-25c9-4813-acd8-cf423be18f35","uuid":"aee7020e-41a8-4a66-8fee-94a2f456e0ec","timestamp":"2026-05-07T05:27:43.029Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/config.rs","content":"//! Translation of `quic/config.h`.\n//!\n//! Demo-application–facing configuration plumbing for quic-core:\n//! the [`Config`] bag of CLI-derived options, the [`OptionId`]\n//! tag identifying each option, and [`Config::create_and_configure`],\n//! the one-shot constructor that turns a populated config into a\n//! fully-wired [`Quic`].\n//!\n//! Phase 4: all function bodies are implemented.\n//!\n//! Pointer-shape decisions for the config struct were guided by\n//! reading `quic/config.c`:\n//!\n//! * Every `char const*` string field that\n//!   `config_clear` `free`s is owned in C (allocated via\n//!   `config_set_string_param`'s `malloc` + `memcpy`).  These map\n//!   to `Option<String>`; `None` substitutes for the C `NULL`\n//!   sentinel that all callers test before use.\n//! * `multipath_alt_config: *mut char` is owned the same way and\n//!   becomes `Option<String>`.\n//! * `ech_target: uint8_t*` plus `ech_target_len` is owned by the\n//!   config (`config_clear` frees it after the base64\n//!   decode in `option_ECH_client`); it becomes\n//!   `Option<Vec<u8>>` with the length implicit in the vector.\n//! * `ticket_encryption_key: const uint8_t*` is *borrowed* in C —\n//!   `config_clear` does not free it.  Phase 1 stores an\n//!   owned `Option<Vec<u8>>` for safety; in v1 only the demo apps\n//!   set this field, and they can supply an owned buffer.  Phase 3\n//!   may revisit if a caller actually relies on aliasing.  The\n//!   paired `ticket_encryption_key_length` field is dropped — its\n//!   value is always implicit in the Vec length.\n//! * Single-bit `unsigned int : 1` flag bitfields (`use_long_log`,\n//!   `do_retry`, …) collapse to individual `bool` fields.  Every C\n//!   call site reads/writes one bit at a time as a Boolean\n//!   (`config->do_retry = 1`), so the\n//!   integer-with-mask-and-shift translation buys nothing here and\n//!   `bitflags!` is overkill for an unrelated set of flags.\n//! * Bitfield `enable_sslkeylog` is gated by\n//!   `#ifndef WITHOUT_SSLKEYLOG` in C.  v1 follows the\n//!   canonical build (the macro is undefined), so the field is\n//!   always present in Rust; a `cfg`-gated variant lands when the\n//!   build options are translated.\n\nuse crate::Error;\nuse crate::Instant;\nuse crate::internal::MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX;\nuse crate::{LossbitVersion, Quic, SpinbitVersion, StreamDataCallback};\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Option identifiers.\n\n/// One identifier per CLI / API option understood by [`Config`].\n///\n/// Mirrors the C `picoquic_option_enum_t`; variant order is\n/// load-bearing — the option dispatch table in `quic/config.c`\n/// indexes by variant — so the discriminants do not get reordered.\n///\n/// [`OptionId::SslKeyLog`] is unconditional here even though the C\n/// enum gates it on `#ifndef WITHOUT_SSLKEYLOG`, matching the\n/// canonical-build behavior; see the module-level docs for the\n/// rationale.\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum OptionId {\n    Cert,\n    Key,\n    ServerPort,\n    ProposedVersion,\n    OutDir,\n    WwwDir,\n    MaxConnections,\n    DoRetry,\n    InitialRandom,\n    ResetSeed,\n    DisablePortBlocking,\n    SolutionDir,\n    CcAlgo,\n    CcOption,\n    Spinbit,\n    Lossbit,\n    Multipath,\n    DestIf,\n    CipherSuite,\n    InitCnxId,\n    LogFile,\n    LongLog,\n    BinlogDir,\n    QlogDir,\n    MtuMax,\n    Sni,\n    Alpn,\n    RootTrustFile,\n    ForceZeroShare,\n    CnxIdLength,\n    NoDisk,\n    IdleTimeout,\n    LargeClientHello,\n    TicketFileName,\n    TokenFileName,\n    SocketBufferSize,\n    PerformanceLog,\n    PreemptiveRepeat,\n    VersionUpgrade,\n    NoGso,\n    BdpFrame,\n    CwinMax,\n    SslKeyLog,\n    AddressDiscovery,\n    EchServer,\n    EchClient,\n    EchInit,\n    FlowControlMax,\n    PreferredV4,\n    PreferredV6,\n    Help,\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Option table (mirrors C static option_table[]).\n\nstruct OptionEntry {\n    id: OptionId,\n    letter: char,\n    name: &'static str,\n    nb_params: usize,\n    param_sample: &'static str,\n    help: &'static str,\n}\n\nstatic OPTION_TABLE: &[OptionEntry] = &[\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::Cert,\n        letter: 'c',\n        name: \"cert\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"file\",\n        help: \"cert file\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::Key,\n        letter: 'k',\n        name: \"key\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"file\",\n        help: \"key file\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::ServerPort,\n        letter: 'p',\n        name: \"port\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"number\",\n        help: \"server port\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::ProposedVersion,\n        letter: 'v',\n        name: \"proposed_version\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"Version proposed by client, e.g. -v ff000012\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::OutDir,\n        letter: 'o',\n        name: \"outdir\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"folder\",\n        help: \"Folder where client writes downloaded files, defaults to current directory.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::WwwDir,\n        letter: 'w',\n        name: \"wwwdir\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"folder\",\n        help: \"Folder containing web pages served by server\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::MaxConnections,\n        letter: 'x',\n        name: \"max_connections\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"number\",\n        help: \"Maximum number of concurrent connections, default 256\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::DoRetry,\n        letter: 'r',\n        name: \"do_retry\",\n        nb_params: 0,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"Do Retry Request\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::InitialRandom,\n        letter: 'R',\n        name: \"initial_random\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"option\",\n        help: \"Randomize packet number spaces: none(0), initial(1, default), all(2).\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::ResetSeed,\n        letter: 's',\n        name: \"reset_seed\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"<32 hex chars>\",\n        help: \"Reset seed\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::DisablePortBlocking,\n        letter: 'X',\n        name: \"disable_block\",\n        nb_params: 0,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"Disable the check for blocked ports\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::SolutionDir,\n        letter: 'S',\n        name: \"solution_dir\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"folder\",\n        help: \"Set the path to the source files to find the default files\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::CcAlgo,\n        letter: 'G',\n        name: \"cc_algo\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"cc_algorithm\",\n        help: \"Use the specified congestion control algorithm. Defaults to bbr.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::CcOption,\n        letter: 'H',\n        name: \"cco\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"option\",\n        help: \"Set option string if required by congestion control algorithm.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::Spinbit,\n        letter: 'P',\n        name: \"spinbit\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"number\",\n        help: \"Set the default spinbit policy\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::Lossbit,\n        letter: 'O',\n        name: \"lossbit\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"number\",\n        help: \"Set the default lossbit policy\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::Multipath,\n        letter: 'M',\n        name: \"multipath\",\n        nb_params: 0,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"Enable QUIC multipath extension\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::DestIf,\n        letter: 'e',\n        name: \"dest_if\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"if\",\n        help: \"Send on interface (default: -1)\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::CipherSuite,\n        letter: 'C',\n        name: \"cipher_suite\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"cipher_suite_id\",\n        help: \"specify cipher suite (e.g. -C 20 = chacha20)\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::InitCnxId,\n        letter: 'i',\n        name: \"cnxid_params\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"per-text-lb-spec\",\n        help: \"See documentation for LB compatible CID configuration\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::LogFile,\n        letter: 'l',\n        name: \"text_log\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"file\",\n        help: \"Log file, Log to stdout if file = \\\"-\\\". No text logging if absent.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::LongLog,\n        letter: 'L',\n        name: \"long_log\",\n        nb_params: 0,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"Log all packets. If absent, log stops after 100 packets.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::BinlogDir,\n        letter: 'b',\n        name: \"binlog_dir\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"folder\",\n        help: \"Binary logging to this directory. No binary logging if absent.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::QlogDir,\n        letter: 'q',\n        name: \"qlog_dir\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"folder\",\n        help: \"Qlog logging to this directory.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::MtuMax,\n        letter: 'm',\n        name: \"mtu_max\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"mtu_max\",\n        help: \"Largest mtu value that can be tried for discovery.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::Sni,\n        letter: 'n',\n        name: \"sni\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"sni\",\n        help: \"sni (default: server name)\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::Alpn,\n        letter: 'a',\n        name: \"alpn\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"alpn\",\n        help: \"alpn (default function of version)\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::RootTrustFile,\n        letter: 't',\n        name: \"root_trust_file\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"file\",\n        help: \"root trust file\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::ForceZeroShare,\n        letter: 'z',\n        name: \"force_zero_share\",\n        nb_params: 0,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"Set TLS zero share behavior on client, to force HRR\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::CnxIdLength,\n        letter: 'I',\n        name: \"cnxid_length\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"length\",\n        help: \"Length of CNX_ID used by the client, default=8\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::IdleTimeout,\n        letter: 'd',\n        name: \"idle_timeout\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"ms\",\n        help: \"Duration of idle timeout in milliseconds (Default 30,000ms)\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::NoDisk,\n        letter: 'D',\n        name: \"no_disk\",\n        nb_params: 0,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"no disk: do not save received files on disk\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::LargeClientHello,\n        letter: 'Q',\n        name: \"large_client_hello\",\n        nb_params: 0,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"send a large client hello in order to test post quantum readiness\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::TicketFileName,\n        letter: 'T',\n        name: \"ticket_file\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"file\",\n        help: \"File storing the session tickets\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::TokenFileName,\n        letter: 'N',\n        name: \"token_file\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"file\",\n        help: \"File storing the new tokens\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::SocketBufferSize,\n        letter: 'B',\n        name: \"so_buf_size\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"number\",\n        help: \"Set buffer size with SO_SNDBUF SO_RCVBUF\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::PerformanceLog,\n        letter: 'F',\n        name: \"log_file_name\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"file\",\n        help: \"Append performance reports to performance log\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::PreemptiveRepeat,\n        letter: 'V',\n        name: \"preemptive_repeat\",\n        nb_params: 0,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"enable preemptive repeat\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::VersionUpgrade,\n        letter: 'U',\n        name: \"version_upgrade\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"Version upgrade if server agrees, e.g. -U 6b3343cf\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::NoGso,\n        letter: '0',\n        name: \"no_gso\",\n        nb_params: 0,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"Do not use UDP GSO or equivalent\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::BdpFrame,\n        letter: 'j',\n        name: \"bdp\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"number\",\n        help: \"use bdp extension frame(1) or don't (0). Default=0\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::CwinMax,\n        letter: 'W',\n        name: \"cwin_max\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"bytes\",\n        help: \"Max value for CWIN. Default=UINT64_MAX\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::SslKeyLog,\n        letter: '8',\n        name: \"sslkeylog\",\n        nb_params: 0,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"Enable SSLKEYLOG\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::AddressDiscovery,\n        letter: 'J',\n        name: \"addr_disc\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"mode\",\n        help: \"provider (0), receiver (1) or both (2).\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::EchServer,\n        letter: 'E',\n        name: \"ech_s\",\n        nb_params: 2,\n        param_sample: \"key config\",\n        help: \"ECH private key file, config file. Default= no ECH on server.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::EchInit,\n        letter: 'y',\n        name: \"ech_init\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"public_name\",\n        help: \"Create an ECH configuration before applying the `ech_s` parameter.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::EchClient,\n        letter: 'K',\n        name: \"ech_c\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"base64\",\n        help: \"ECH configuration for the client connection, base64 encoded.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::FlowControlMax,\n        letter: 'Z',\n        name: \"flow_control_max\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"bytes\",\n        help: \"Set the flow control's initial max data.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::PreferredV4,\n        letter: '4',\n        name: \"preferred_v4\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"ip[:port]\",\n        help: \"Preferred address for v4 connections.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::PreferredV6,\n        letter: '6',\n        name: \"preferred_v6\",\n        nb_params: 1,\n        param_sample: \"ipv6[:port]\",\n        help: \"Preferred address for v6 connections.\",\n    },\n    OptionEntry {\n        id: OptionId::Help,\n        letter: 'h',\n        name: \"help\",\n        nb_params: 0,\n        param_sample: \"\",\n        help: \"This help message\",\n    },\n];\n\nfn parse_hex_version(s: &str) -> u32 {\n    u32::from_str_radix(s, 16).unwrap_or(0)\n}\n\nfn base64_decode(s: &str) -> Result<Vec<u8>, Error> {\n    let mut table = [0xFFu8; 256];\n    for (i, &c) in b\"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/\"\n        .iter()\n        .enumerate()\n    {\n        table[c as usize] = i as u8;\n    }\n    let bytes: Vec<u8> = s.bytes().filter(|&c| c != b'=').collect();\n    let mut out = Vec::new();\n    for chunk in bytes.chunks(4) {\n        let mut v = [0u8; 4];\n        let n = chunk.len();\n        for (i, &b) in chunk.iter().enumerate() {\n            let x = table[b as usize];\n            if x == 0xFF {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            v[i] = x;\n        }\n        out.push((v[0] << 2) | (v[1] >> 4));\n        if n >= 3 {\n            out.push((v[1] << 4) | (v[2] >> 2));\n        }\n        if n == 4 {\n            out.push((v[2] << 6) | v[3]);\n        }\n    }\n    Ok(out)\n}\n\nfn option_entry(id: OptionId) -> Option<&'static OptionEntry> {\n    OPTION_TABLE.iter().find(|e| e.id == id)\n}\n\nfn option_entry_by_letter(letter: char) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> {\n    OPTION_TABLE\n        .iter()\n        .enumerate()\n        .find(|(_, e)| e.letter == letter)\n}\n\nfn option_entry_by_name(name: &str) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> {\n    OPTION_TABLE\n        .iter()\n        .enumerate()\n        .find(|(_, e)| e.name == name)\n}\n\nfn apply_option(config: &mut Config, entry: &OptionEntry, params: &[&str]) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    let p0 = params.first().copied();\n    let p1 = params.get(1).copied();\n    match entry.id {\n        OptionId::Cert => {\n            config.server_cert_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::Key => {\n            config.server_key_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::ServerPort => {\n            config.set_port(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?)?;\n        }\n        OptionId::ProposedVersion => {\n            let v = parse_hex_version(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?);\n            if v == 0 {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.proposed_version = v;\n        }\n        OptionId::OutDir => {\n            config.out_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::WwwDir => {\n            config.www_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::MaxConnections => {\n            let v: i32 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            if v <= 0 {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.nb_connections = v as u32;\n        }\n        OptionId::DoRetry => {\n            config.do_retry = true;\n        }\n        OptionId::InitialRandom => {\n            let v: i32 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            if !(0..=2).contains(&v) {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.initial_random = v as u32;\n        }\n        OptionId::ResetSeed => {\n            config.has_reset_seed = true;\n            let n =\n                crate::utils::parse_hexa(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?, &mut config.reset_seed);\n            if n != config.reset_seed.len() {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n        }\n        OptionId::DisablePortBlocking => {\n            config.disable_port_blocking = true;\n        }\n        OptionId::SslKeyLog => {\n            config.enable_sslkeylog = true;\n        }\n        OptionId::SolutionDir => {\n            config.solution_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::CcAlgo => {\n            config.cc_algo_id = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::CcOption => {\n            config.cc_algo_option_string = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::Spinbit => {\n            let v: i32 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            config.spinbit_policy = match v {\n                0 => SpinbitVersion::Basic,\n                1 => SpinbitVersion::Random,\n                2 => SpinbitVersion::Null,\n                3 => SpinbitVersion::On,\n                _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n            };\n        }\n        OptionId::Lossbit => {\n            let v: i32 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            config.lossbit_policy = match v {\n                0 => LossbitVersion::None,\n                1 => LossbitVersion::SendOnly,\n                2 => LossbitVersion::SendReceive,\n                _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n            };\n        }\n        OptionId::Multipath => {\n            config.multipath_option = 1;\n        }\n        OptionId::DestIf => {\n            config.dest_if = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n        }\n        OptionId::CipherSuite => {\n            config.cipher_suite_id = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n        }\n        OptionId::InitCnxId => {\n            config.connection_id_cbdata = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::LogFile => {\n            config.log_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::LongLog => {\n            config.use_long_log = true;\n        }\n        OptionId::BinlogDir => {\n            config.bin_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::QlogDir => {\n            config.qlog_dir = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::MtuMax => {\n            let v: i32 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            if v <= 0 || v > crate::internal::MAX_PACKET_SIZE as i32 {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.mtu_max = v;\n        }\n        OptionId::Sni => {\n            config.sni = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::Alpn => {\n            config.alpn = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::RootTrustFile => {\n            config.root_trust_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::ForceZeroShare => {\n            config.force_zero_share = true;\n        }\n        OptionId::CnxIdLength => {\n            let v: i32 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            if v < 0 || v > crate::CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE as i32 {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.connection_id_length = v;\n        }\n        OptionId::IdleTimeout => {\n            let v: i32 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            if v < 0 {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.idle_timeout = v;\n        }\n        OptionId::NoDisk => {\n            config.no_disk = true;\n        }\n        OptionId::LargeClientHello => {\n            config.large_client_hello = true;\n        }\n        OptionId::TicketFileName => {\n            config.ticket_file_name = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::TokenFileName => {\n            config.token_file_name = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::SocketBufferSize => {\n            let v: i32 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            if v < 0 {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.socket_buffer_size = v;\n        }\n        OptionId::PerformanceLog => {\n            config.performance_log = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::PreemptiveRepeat => {\n            config.do_preemptive_repeat = true;\n        }\n        OptionId::VersionUpgrade => {\n            let v = parse_hex_version(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?);\n            if v == 0 {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.desired_version = v;\n        }\n        OptionId::NoGso => {\n            config.do_not_use_gso = true;\n        }\n        OptionId::BdpFrame => {\n            let v: i32 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            if !(0..=1).contains(&v) {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.bdp_frame_option = v;\n        }\n        OptionId::CwinMax => {\n            let v: i64 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            if v < 0 {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.cwin_max = if v == 0 { u64::MAX } else { v as u64 };\n        }\n        OptionId::AddressDiscovery => {\n            let v: i32 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            if !(0..=2).contains(&v) {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.address_discovery_mode = v + 1;\n        }\n        OptionId::EchServer => {\n            config.ech_key_file = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n            if let Some(s) = p1 {\n                config.ech_config_file = Some(s.to_string());\n            }\n        }\n        OptionId::EchInit => {\n            config.ech_public_name = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::EchClient => {\n            let s = p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            if s == \"-\" {\n                config.ech_target = None;\n            } else {\n                config.ech_target = Some(base64_decode(s).map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?);\n            }\n        }\n        OptionId::FlowControlMax => {\n            let v: i64 = p0\n                .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?\n                .parse()\n                .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n            if v < 0 {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            config.flow_control_max = v as u64;\n        }\n        OptionId::PreferredV4 => {\n            config.preferred_address_v4 = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::PreferredV6 => {\n            config.preferred_address_v6 = Some(p0.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?.to_string());\n        }\n        OptionId::Help => {\n            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n        }\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}\n\nfn collect_params<'a>(\n    entry: &OptionEntry,\n    p_optind: &mut usize,\n    argv: &[&'a str],\n    optarg: Option<&'a str>,\n) -> Result<Vec<&'a str>, Error> {\n    let mut params = Vec::new();\n    if entry.nb_params > 0 {\n        params.push(optarg.ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?);\n        let mut nb = 1;\n        while nb < entry.nb_params {\n            if *p_optind >= argv.len() {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n            }\n            params.push(argv[*p_optind]);\n            *p_optind += 1;\n            nb += 1;\n        }\n    }\n    Ok(params)\n}\n\nfn parse_option_string(opt_string: &str) -> Option<(usize, &'static OptionEntry)> {\n    if opt_string.starts_with(\"--\") && opt_string.len() > 2 {\n        option_entry_by_name(&opt_string[2..])\n    } else if opt_string.starts_with('-') && opt_string.len() == 2 {\n        opt_string.chars().nth(1).and_then(option_entry_by_letter)\n    } else {\n        None\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Configuration struct.\n\n/// Configuration bag for a QUIC context, populated from CLI flags\n/// (via [`Config::command_line`]) or directly (via\n/// [`Config::set_option`]) and consumed by\n/// [`Config::create_and_configure`].\n///\n/// Mirrors the C `picoquic_quic_config_t` field-for-field;\n/// `repr(C)` is dropped because the struct never crosses an\n/// external boundary.  See the module-level docs for the\n/// pointer-shape rationale.\n///\n/// `Default` produces the documented C defaults:\n/// `nb_connections = 256`, `connection_id_length = -1`, `cwin_max =\n/// u64::MAX`, idle timeout from `MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX`, etc.  This\n/// folds the C `picoquic_config_init` step into the constructor —\n/// the C `config_clear` (which `free`s every owned string) collapses\n/// to `Drop`, and resetting a config to defaults is just\n/// `*config = Config::default()`.\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub struct Config {\n    pub nb_connections: u32,\n    pub solution_dir: Option<String>,\n    pub server_cert_file: Option<String>,\n    pub server_key_file: Option<String>,\n    pub log_file: Option<String>,\n    pub bin_dir: Option<String>,\n    pub qlog_dir: Option<String>,\n    pub performance_log: Option<String>,\n    pub server_port: u16,\n    pub local_port: u16,\n    /// Whether the public port is shared with sibling threads\n    /// (`SO_REUSEPORT`).  C: `int is_port_shared`, used as a\n    /// Boolean flag.\n    pub is_port_shared: bool,\n    pub nb_threads: i32,\n    pub dest_if: i32,\n    pub mtu_max: i32,\n    /// `-1` is the C \"unset\" sentinel applied by [`Self::init`];\n    /// values `>= 0` set the connection-ID length explicitly.  Kept\n    /// as `i32` rather than `Option<u8>` for source-level parity\n    /// with the C body.\n    pub connection_id_length: i32,\n    pub idle_timeout: i32,\n    pub socket_buffer_size: i32,\n    pub cc_algo_id: Option<String>,\n    pub cc_algo_option_string: Option<String>,\n    pub connection_id_cbdata: Option<String>,\n    pub spinbit_policy: SpinbitVersion,\n    pub lossbit_policy: LossbitVersion,\n    pub multipath_option: i32,\n    pub multipath_alt_config: Option<String>,\n    pub bdp_frame_option: i32,\n    pub cwin_max: u64,\n    pub address_discovery_mode: i32,\n\n    // Common flags.\n    pub initial_random: u32,\n    pub use_long_log: bool,\n    pub do_preemptive_repeat: bool,\n    pub do_not_use_gso: bool,\n    pub disable_port_blocking: bool,\n    /// Originally bitfield-gated by `#ifndef\n    /// WITHOUT_SSLKEYLOG`; v1 follows the canonical build\n    /// (always defined), so the field is unconditional here.\n    pub enable_sslkeylog: bool,\n\n    // Server only.\n    pub www_dir: Option<String>,\n    pub reset_seed: [u8; 16],\n    /// Borrowed in C (`config_clear` does not free it); owned\n    /// `Vec<u8>` here for safety.  The C\n    /// `ticket_encryption_key_length` field is dropped — its value\n    /// is always `ticket_encryption_key.as_ref().map_or(0, Vec::len)`.\n    pub ticket_encryption_key: Option<Vec<u8>>,\n\n    // Server flags.\n    pub do_retry: bool,\n    pub has_reset_seed: bool,\n\n    // Client only.\n    pub ticket_file_name: Option<String>,\n    pub token_file_name: Option<String>,\n    pub sni: Option<String>,\n    pub alpn: Option<String>,\n    pub out_dir: Option<String>,\n    pub root_trust_file: Option<String>,\n    pub cipher_suite_id: i32,\n    pub proposed_version: u32,\n    pub desired_version: u32,\n    pub force_zero_share: bool,\n    pub no_disk: bool,\n    pub large_client_hello: bool,\n\n    // ECH parameters for server.\n    pub ech_key_file: Option<String>,\n    pub ech_config_file: Option<String>,\n    pub ech_public_name: Option<String>,\n    /// ECH parameter for the client, base64-decoded.  Owned by\n    /// the config — `config_clear` frees it in C.  The C\n    /// `ech_target_len` field is dropped — its value is always\n    /// `ech_target.as_ref().map_or(0, Vec::len)`.\n    pub ech_target: Option<Vec<u8>>,\n\n    pub flow_control_max: u64,\n\n    // Preferred address, encoded as strings.\n    pub preferred_address_v4: Option<String>,\n    pub preferred_address_v6: Option<String>,\n}\n\nimpl Default for Config {\n    /// Build a fresh config with the documented C defaults.  C:\n    /// `picoquic_config_init` (which the C body invoked after a\n    /// zero-initialising `memset`).\n    fn default() -> Self {\n        Config {\n            nb_connections: 256,\n            solution_dir: None,\n            server_cert_file: None,\n            server_key_file: None,\n            log_file: None,\n            bin_dir: None,\n            qlog_dir: None,\n            performance_log: None,\n            server_port: 0,\n            local_port: 0,\n            is_port_shared: false,\n            nb_threads: 0,\n            dest_if: 0,\n            mtu_max: 0,\n            connection_id_length: -1,\n            idle_timeout: (MICROSEC_HANDSHAKE_MAX.ticks() / 1000) as i32,\n            socket_buffer_size: 0,\n            cc_algo_id: None,\n            cc_algo_option_string: None,\n            connection_id_cbdata: None,\n            spinbit_policy: SpinbitVersion::default(),\n            lossbit_policy: LossbitVersion::default(),\n            multipath_option: 0,\n            multipath_alt_config: None,\n            bdp_frame_option: 0,\n            cwin_max: u64::MAX,\n            address_discovery_mode: 0,\n            initial_random: 3,\n            use_long_log: false,\n            do_preemptive_repeat: false,\n            do_not_use_gso: false,\n            disable_port_blocking: false,\n            enable_sslkeylog: false,\n            www_dir: None,\n            reset_seed: [0; 16],\n            ticket_encryption_key: None,\n            do_retry: false,\n            has_reset_seed: false,\n            ticket_file_name: None,\n            token_file_name: None,\n            sni: None,\n            alpn: None,\n            out_dir: None,\n            root_trust_file: None,\n            cipher_suite_id: 0,\n            proposed_version: 0,\n            desired_version: 0,\n            force_zero_share: false,\n            no_disk: false,\n            large_client_hello: false,\n            ech_key_file: None,\n            ech_config_file: None,\n            ech_public_name: None,\n            ech_target: None,\n            flow_control_max: 0,\n            preferred_address_v4: None,\n            preferred_address_v6: None,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Config {\n    /// Apply one option, selected by `option`, to the config.\n    /// C: `picoquic_config_set_option`.\n    ///\n    /// `value` is optional — flag-style options ([`OptionId::DoRetry`],\n    /// [`OptionId::LongLog`], …) ignore it; value-style options\n    /// require it and return `Err` when it is missing or malformed.\n    ///\n    /// The C signature returned `int` (`0` ↔ `Ok`, `-1` ↔ `Err`);\n    /// mapped to `Result<(), Error>`.\n    pub fn set_option(&mut self, option: OptionId, value: Option<&str>) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let entry = option_entry(option).ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n        let params: &[&str] = match value {\n            Some(v) => &[v],\n            None => &[],\n        };\n        apply_option(self, entry, params)\n    }\n\n    /// Dispatch one option from a single-character flag (`-x`).\n    /// C: `picoquic_config_command_line`.\n    ///\n    /// `p_optind` advances past any extra arguments consumed beyond\n    /// the inline `optarg`, mirroring the C in/out parameter so that\n    /// an outer getopt-style loop stays in sync.\n    ///\n    /// `argv` is a borrowed slice of borrowed strings — the C caller\n    /// (`first` etc.) owns the argument vector for the program\n    /// lifetime, so a borrow is safe.  The C `int argc` parameter is\n    /// dropped (implicit in `argv.len()`).\n    pub fn command_line(\n        &mut self,\n        opt: char,\n        p_optind: &mut usize,\n        argv: &[&str],\n        optarg: Option<&str>,\n    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let (_, entry) = option_entry_by_letter(opt).ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n        let params = collect_params(entry, p_optind, argv, optarg)?;\n        apply_option(self, entry, &params)\n    }\n\n    /// Like [`Self::command_line`] but accepts both single-character\n    /// (`-x`) and long-form (`--name`) option strings; the leading\n    /// dashes are part of `opt_string`, matching the C contract.\n    /// C: `picoquic_config_command_line_ex`.\n    pub fn command_line_ex(\n        &mut self,\n        opt_string: &str,\n        p_optind: &mut usize,\n        argv: &[&str],\n        optarg: Option<&str>,\n    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let (_, entry) = parse_option_string(opt_string).ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n        let params = collect_params(entry, p_optind, argv, optarg)?;\n        apply_option(self, entry, &params)\n    }\n\n    /// Build the getopt-style option string from the dispatch table\n    /// in `config.c` — one letter per option, with `:` after each\n    /// option that takes an argument.  C:\n    /// `picoquic_config_option_letters`.\n    ///\n    /// The C signature wrote into a caller-supplied buffer\n    /// (`option_string`, `string_max`) and reported the populated\n    /// length via `*string_length`.  The Rust wrapper owns the\n    /// buffer and returns it directly, so the buffer-too-small\n    /// failure mode disappears.\n    pub fn option_letters() -> String {\n        let mut s = String::new();\n        for e in OPTION_TABLE {\n            s.push(e.letter);\n            if e.nb_params > 0 {\n                s.push(':');\n            }\n        }\n        s\n    }\n\n    /// Write the option help to a [`core::fmt::Write`] sink.\n    /// C: `picoquic_config_usage_file`.\n    ///\n    /// The C parameter was `FILE*`; the Rust translation accepts\n    /// any sink (a `String` buffer, the stdout/stderr handles under\n    /// the `std` feature, or a custom writer) so the function\n    /// stays `no_std`-friendly.\n    pub fn write_usage(w: &mut dyn core::fmt::Write) {\n        let _ = w.write_str(\"Picoquic options:\\n\");\n        for e in OPTION_TABLE {\n            let _ = write!(w, \"  -{} {}\", e.letter, e.param_sample);\n            let pad = 12usize.saturating_sub(e.param_sample.len());\n            for _ in 0..pad {\n                let _ = w.write_char(' ');\n            }\n            let _ = writeln!(w, \" {}\", e.help);\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Print the option help to stderr.  C: `picoquic_config_usage`.\n    ///\n    /// Routes through an intermediate `String` buffer then `eprint!`.\n    pub fn print_usage() {\n        let mut buf = String::new();\n        Self::write_usage(&mut buf);\n        eprint!(\"{}\", buf);\n    }\n\n    /// Parse a port-configuration string into `server_port`,\n    /// `local_port`, `is_port_shared`, and `nb_threads`.\n    /// C: `config_set_port` (internal, called from the `-p` option\n    /// handler in `picoquic/config.c`).\n    ///\n    /// Accepted formats:\n    /// - `\"\"` / `\"0\"` — clear all (port 0, not shared)\n    /// - `\"4433\"` — server port only\n    /// - `\"443:4434\"` — server:local\n    /// - `\"S4433\"` — shared server port\n    /// - `\"S443:4434*256\"` — shared server:local, 256 threads\n    /// - `\"4433*7\"` — server port, 7 threads\n    ///\n    /// Returns `Err` when any token cannot be parsed or a port value\n    /// exceeds 65535.\n    pub fn set_port(&mut self, port_string: &str) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let bytes = port_string.as_bytes();\n        let mut i = 0;\n        let mut is_port_shared = false;\n        let mut p1: i32 = 0;\n        let mut p2: i32 = 0;\n        let mut nb_threads: i32 = 0;\n\n        if i < bytes.len() && bytes[i] == b'S' {\n            is_port_shared = true;\n            i += 1;\n        }\n        while i < bytes.len() && bytes[i].is_ascii_digit() {\n            p1 = p1 * 10 + (bytes[i] - b'0') as i32;\n            i += 1;\n        }\n        if i < bytes.len() && bytes[i] == b':' {\n            i += 1;\n            while i < bytes.len() && bytes[i].is_ascii_digit() {\n                p2 = p2 * 10 + (bytes[i] - b'0') as i32;\n                i += 1;\n            }\n        }\n        if i < bytes.len() && bytes[i] == b'*' {\n            i += 1;\n            while i < bytes.len() && bytes[i].is_ascii_digit() {\n                nb_threads = nb_threads * 10 + (bytes[i] - b'0') as i32;\n                i += 1;\n            }\n        }\n        if i != bytes.len() || !(0..=65535).contains(&p1) || !(0..=65535).contains(&p2) {\n            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n        }\n        self.server_port = p1 as u16;\n        self.local_port = p2 as u16;\n        self.is_port_shared = is_port_shared;\n        self.nb_threads = nb_threads;\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    /// Build a fully-configured QUIC context from this config plus\n    /// an application-supplied callback.  C:\n    /// `picoquic_create_and_configure`.\n    ///\n    /// Returns `None` when context creation fails (the C side\n    /// returned `NULL`).\n    ///\n    /// Pointer-shape choices, derived from the C signature and the\n    /// body in `config.c`:\n    ///\n    /// * `picoquic_quic_config_t* config` is consumed-borrowed\n    ///   (`&mut self`): the body reads every field and may set up\n    ///   downstream owned state, but it does not free the struct\n    ///   itself — ownership stays with the caller.\n    /// * `default_callback_fn` + `default_callback_ctx` collapse to\n    ///   one `Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>` per the\n    ///   function-pointers-map-to-traits rule, with the `void*`\n    ///   context folded into the trait implementor's state.  `None`\n    ///   matches the C \"no default callback\" case where the function\n    ///   pointer was `NULL`.\n    /// * `p_simulated_time: *mut u64` carries simulated wall time for\n    ///   tests; the C QUIC context retains the pointer across calls,\n    ///   so an `&mut u64` borrow expresses the contract directly.\n    ///   Phase 3 may revisit (e.g. with a clock trait) once the QUIC\n    ///   context type is real.\n    pub fn create_and_configure(\n        &mut self,\n        default_callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n        current_time: Instant,\n        _p_simulated_time: Option<&mut u64>,\n    ) -> Option<Box<Quic>> {\n        let reset_seed = if self.has_reset_seed {\n            self.reset_seed\n        } else {\n            [0u8; 16]\n        };\n\n        let mut quic = Quic::new(\n            self.nb_connections,\n            self.server_cert_file.as_deref(),\n            self.server_key_file.as_deref(),\n            self.root_trust_file.as_deref(),\n            self.alpn.as_deref(),\n            default_callback,\n            None,\n            reset_seed,\n            current_time,\n            self.ticket_file_name.as_deref(),\n            self.ticket_encryption_key.as_deref(),\n        )?;\n\n        if self.do_retry {\n            quic.set_cookie_mode(1);\n        } else {\n            quic.set_cookie_mode(2);\n        }\n\n        if let Some(ref cc_id) = self.cc_algo_id {\n            let _ = quic.set_default_congestion_algorithm_by_name(cc_id);\n        }\n\n        let _ = quic.set_default_spinbit_policy(self.spinbit_policy);\n        quic.set_default_lossbit_policy(self.lossbit_policy);\n        quic.set_default_multipath_option(self.multipath_option);\n        quic.set_default_idle_timeout(crate::Duration::from_ticks(self.idle_timeout as u64 * 1000));\n        quic.set_cwin_max(self.cwin_max);\n        quic.set_default_address_discovery_mode(self.address_discovery_mode);\n\n        if let Some(ref token_file) = self.token_file_name {\n            let _ = quic.load_retry_tokens(token_file);\n        }\n\n        if self.force_zero_share {\n            quic.client_zero_share = true;\n        }\n\n        if self.mtu_max > 0 {\n            quic.set_mtu_max(self.mtu_max as u32);\n        }\n\n        if self.connection_id_length != -1 {\n            let _ = quic.set_default_connection_id_length(self.connection_id_length as u8);\n        }\n\n        quic.set_padding_policy(39, 128);\n\n        if let Some(ref bin_dir) = self.bin_dir {\n            let _ = quic.set_binlog(Some(bin_dir.as_str()));\n        }\n\n        if let Some(ref qlog_dir) = self.qlog_dir {\n            let _ = quic.set_qlog(qlog_dir.as_str());\n        }\n\n        if let Some(ref log_file) = self.log_file {\n            let _ = quic.set_textlog(Some(log_file.as_str()));\n        }\n\n        quic.set_log_level(if self.use_long_log { 1 } else { 0 });\n        quic.set_preemptive_repeat_policy(self.do_preemptive_repeat);\n        quic.set_port_blocking_disabled(self.disable_port_blocking);\n        quic.set_sslkeylog_enabled(self.enable_sslkeylog);\n\n        if self.initial_random <= 2 {\n            quic.set_random_initial(self.initial_random as i32);\n        }\n\n        if self.cipher_suite_id != 0 {\n            let iana_code = match self.cipher_suite_id {\n                20 => crate::CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256,\n                128 => crate::AES_128_GCM_SHA256,\n                256 => crate::AES_256_GCM_SHA384,\n                v => v as u16,\n            };\n            let _ = quic.set_cipher_suite(iana_code);\n        }\n\n        if self.do_retry {\n            quic.set_cookie_mode(1);\n        } else {\n            quic.set_cookie_mode(2);\n        }\n\n        quic.set_default_bdp_frame_option(self.bdp_frame_option != 0);\n\n        let mut failed = false;\n\n        if let Some(ref public_name) = self.ech_public_name {\n            if self.ech_key_file.is_none() || self.ech_config_file.is_none() {\n                // key file or config file not specified — cannot create ECH config\n            } else {\n                let key_file = self.ech_key_file.as_deref().unwrap();\n                let cfg_file = self.ech_config_file.as_deref().unwrap();\n                if crate::ech_create_config_file(public_name, key_file, cfg_file).is_err() {\n                    failed = true;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        if !failed\n            && (self.ech_key_file.is_some() || self.ech_target.is_some())\n            && quic\n                .ech_configure(\n                    self.ech_key_file.as_deref(),\n                    self.ech_config_file.as_deref(),\n                )\n                .is_err()\n        {\n            failed = true;\n        }\n\n        if !failed && self.flow_control_max > 0 {\n            quic.set_max_data_control(self.flow_control_max);\n        }\n\n        if failed { None } else { Some(quic) }\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod test {}\n","numLines":1404,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1404}}}
