{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S4N5FgzZkJETmNfpyjWhkz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/*\n2\t* Author: Christian Huitema\n3\t* Copyright (c) 2025, Private Octopus, Inc.\n4\t* All rights reserved.\n5\t*\n6\t* Permission to use, copy, modify, and distribute this software for any\n7\t* purpose with or without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above\n8\t* copyright notice and this permission notice appear in all copies.\n9\t*\n10\t* THIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED BY THE COPYRIGHT HOLDERS AND CONTRIBUTORS \"AS IS\" AND\n11\t* ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED\n12\t* WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE ARE\n13\t* DISCLAIMED. IN NO EVENT SHALL Private Octopus, Inc. BE LIABLE FOR ANY\n14\t* DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES\n15\t* (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES;\n16\t* LOSS OF USE, DATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND\n17\t* ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT\n18\t* (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS\n19\t* SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.\n20\t*/\n21\t\n22\t#include \"picoquic_internal.h\"\n23\t#include <stdlib.h>\n24\t#include <string.h>\n25\t#include \"cc_common.h\"\n26\t\n27\t/* C4 algorithm is a work in progress. We start with some simple principles:\n28\t* - Track delays, but this expose issue when competing with Cubic\n29\t* - Compete with Cubic: fallback to BBRv1, best of last 6 epochs, ignore delays, losses.\n30\t* - Stopping the compete mode? When the delay becomes acceptable?\n31\t* - App limited mode: freeze the parameters? Do probe on search?\n32\t* - Probing mode: probe for one RTT, recover for one RTT, assess after recover.\n33\t* - Probing interval: Fibonacci sequence, up to 16 or 17? 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13\n34\t* - Tuning the interval: no bw increase => larger, bw increase => sooner, how soon?\n35\t* - stopping the compete mode: ECN? ECN as signal that the bottleneck is actively managed.\n36\t* - compete with self? Maybe introduce some random behavior.\n37\t* Principles were later revised to track data rate and max RTT.\n38\t */\n39\t\n40\t/* States of C4:\n41\t* \n42\t* Initial.   Similar to Hystart for now, as a place holder.\n43\t* Recovery.  After an event, freeze the parameters for one RTT. This is the time\n44\t*            to measure whether a previous push was a success.\n45\t* Cruising.  For N intervals. Be ready to notice congestion, or change in conditions.\n46\t*            We should define N as x*log(cwin / cwin_min), so connections sending\n47\t*            lots of data wait a bit longer, which should improve fairness.\n48\t*            Question: is this \"N intervals\" or \"some amount of data sent\"?\n49\t*            the latter is better for the fairness issue.\n50\t* Pushing.   For one RTT. Transmit at higher rate, to probe the network, then\n51\t*            move to \"cruising\". Higher rate should be 25% higher, to probe\n52\t*            without creating big queues.\n53\t* Slowdown.  Periodic slowdown to 1/2 the nominal CWIN, in order to reset\n54\t*            the min delay.\n55\t* Checking:  Post slowdown. use nominal CWND until the min CWND is\n56\t*            verified.\n57\t* \n58\t* Transitions:\n59\t*            initial to recovery -- similar to hystart for now.\n60\t*            recovery to initial -- if measurements show increase in data rate compared to era.\n61\t*            recovery to cruising -- at the end of period.\n62\t*            cruising, pushing to recovery -- if excess delay, loss or ECN\n63\t*            pushing to recovery -- at end of period.\n64\t*            to slowdown..\n65\t* \n66\t* \n67\t* State variables:\n68\t* - CWIN. Main control variable.\n69\t* - Sequence number of first packet sent in epoch. Epoch ends when this is acknowledged.\n70\t* - Observed data rate. Measured at the end of epoch N, reflects setting at epoch N-1.\n71\t* - Average rate of EC marking\n72\t* - Average rate of Packet loss\n73\t* - Average rate of excess delay\n74\t* - Number of cruising bytes sent.\n75\t* - Cruising bytes target before transition to push\n76\t* - RTT min\n77\t */\n78\t\n79\t /* The probe level is used to set the probing rate during the \"push\" phase.\n80\t *\n81\t * The probe level is set to 1 when entering the initial phase.\n82\t *\n83\t * It is computed by an adaptive mechanism:\n84\t *\n85\t * - increase the level by 1 if the previous push was successful\n86\t * - decrease the level by 1 if the previous push was not successful, down to level 1.\n87\t * - set the level to zero if the push generated heavy packet loss or CE marks.\n88\t *\n89\t * The probe level is at most 3. An increase above 3 is equivalent to a decision\n90\t * to reenter the initial phase.\n91\t *\n92\t * Probing rate and number of cruising cycles are function of the level:\n93\t *  - Level 0: push rate 3,125%, 4 cycles before push\n94\t *  - Level 1: push rate 6.25%, 4 cycles before push\n95\t *  - Level 2: push rate 25%, 4 cycles before push\n96\t *  - Level 3: push rate 25%, 1 cycle before push\n97\t */\n98\t\n99\t#define C4_WITH_LOGGING\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"589969e0-25c9-4813-acd8-cf423be18f35","uuid":"1132711a-579d-440c-bb82-e2213719e339","timestamp":"2026-05-07T05:27:49.504Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/picoquic/c4.c","content":"/*\n* Author: Christian Huitema\n* Copyright (c) 2025, Private Octopus, Inc.\n* All rights reserved.\n*\n* Permission to use, copy, modify, and distribute this software for any\n* purpose with or without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above\n* copyright notice and this permission notice appear in all copies.\n*\n* THIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED BY THE COPYRIGHT HOLDERS AND CONTRIBUTORS \"AS IS\" AND\n* ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED\n* WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE ARE\n* DISCLAIMED. IN NO EVENT SHALL Private Octopus, Inc. BE LIABLE FOR ANY\n* DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES\n* (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES;\n* LOSS OF USE, DATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND\n* ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT\n* (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS\n* SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.\n*/\n\n#include \"picoquic_internal.h\"\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include \"cc_common.h\"\n\n/* C4 algorithm is a work in progress. We start with some simple principles:\n* - Track delays, but this expose issue when competing with Cubic\n* - Compete with Cubic: fallback to BBRv1, best of last 6 epochs, ignore delays, losses.\n* - Stopping the compete mode? When the delay becomes acceptable?\n* - App limited mode: freeze the parameters? Do probe on search?\n* - Probing mode: probe for one RTT, recover for one RTT, assess after recover.\n* - Probing interval: Fibonacci sequence, up to 16 or 17? 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13\n* - Tuning the interval: no bw increase => larger, bw increase => sooner, how soon?\n* - stopping the compete mode: ECN? ECN as signal that the bottleneck is actively managed.\n* - compete with self? Maybe introduce some random behavior.\n* Principles were later revised to track data rate and max RTT.\n */\n\n/* States of C4:\n* \n* Initial.   Similar to Hystart for now, as a place holder.\n* Recovery.  After an event, freeze the parameters for one RTT. This is the time\n*            to measure whether a previous push was a success.\n* Cruising.  For N intervals. Be ready to notice congestion, or change in conditions.\n*            We should define N as x*log(cwin / cwin_min), so connections sending\n*            lots of data wait a bit longer, which should improve fairness.\n*            Question: is this \"N intervals\" or \"some amount of data sent\"?\n*            the latter is better for the fairness issue.\n* Pushing.   For one RTT. Transmit at higher rate, to probe the network, then\n*            move to \"cruising\". Higher rate should be 25% higher, to probe\n*            without creating big queues.\n* Slowdown.  Periodic slowdown to 1/2 the nominal CWIN, in order to reset\n*            the min delay.\n* Checking:  Post slowdown. use nominal CWND until the min CWND is\n*            verified.\n* \n* Transitions:\n*            initial to recovery -- similar to hystart for now.\n*            recovery to initial -- if measurements show increase in data rate compared to era.\n*            recovery to cruising -- at the end of period.\n*            cruising, pushing to recovery -- if excess delay, loss or ECN\n*            pushing to recovery -- at end of period.\n*            to slowdown..\n* \n* \n* State variables:\n* - CWIN. Main control variable.\n* - Sequence number of first packet sent in epoch. Epoch ends when this is acknowledged.\n* - Observed data rate. Measured at the end of epoch N, reflects setting at epoch N-1.\n* - Average rate of EC marking\n* - Average rate of Packet loss\n* - Average rate of excess delay\n* - Number of cruising bytes sent.\n* - Cruising bytes target before transition to push\n* - RTT min\n */\n\n /* The probe level is used to set the probing rate during the \"push\" phase.\n *\n * The probe level is set to 1 when entering the initial phase.\n *\n * It is computed by an adaptive mechanism:\n *\n * - increase the level by 1 if the previous push was successful\n * - decrease the level by 1 if the previous push was not successful, down to level 1.\n * - set the level to zero if the push generated heavy packet loss or CE marks.\n *\n * The probe level is at most 3. An increase above 3 is equivalent to a decision\n * to reenter the initial phase.\n *\n * Probing rate and number of cruising cycles are function of the level:\n *  - Level 0: push rate 3,125%, 4 cycles before push\n *  - Level 1: push rate 6.25%, 4 cycles before push\n *  - Level 2: push rate 25%, 4 cycles before push\n *  - Level 3: push rate 25%, 1 cycle before push\n */\n\n#define C4_WITH_LOGGING\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1140}}}
