{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D8jeBhwYCdaPuJ8z25bWmN","type":"tool_result","content":"870\t/// Under multipath each path has its own context; under single-path\n871\t/// only the default path (`unique_path_id == 0`, corresponding to\n872\t/// `cnx->path[0]` in C) participates in ECN tracking — other paths\n873\t/// return `None`.\n874\t///\n875\t/// Note: in C the path held a back-pointer to its connection\n876\t/// (`path_x->cnx`); in Rust there is no back-pointer, so the caller\n877\t/// must supply both `connection` and `path_x`.\n878\tpub fn access_ecn_packet_context<'a>(\n879\t    connection: &'a Connection,\n880\t    path_x: &'a Path,\n881\t) -> Option<&'a PacketContextState> {\n882\t    if connection.is_multipath_enabled {\n883\t        Some(&path_x.pkt_ctx)\n884\t    } else if path_x.unique_path_id != 0 {\n885\t        // Non-default path in single-path mode: ECN counts are not\n886\t        // tracked per-path here; the caller should use the default path.\n887\t        None\n888\t    } else {\n889\t        Some(&connection.pkt_ctx[PacketContext::Application as usize])\n890\t    }\n891\t}\n892\t\n893\t/// C: `BBRSetRsFromAckState` (picoquic/bbr.c:2363)\n894\t///\n895\t/// Convert the `PerAckState` delivered by picoquic's ACK-processing\n896\t/// layer into the `BbrPerAckState` (\"rs\") struct used throughout BBRv3.\n897\t/// Delivery rate is taken from the path's bandwidth estimate when\n898\t/// available; otherwise it is derived from bytes-delivered / RTT; as a\n899\t/// last resort a 40 kBps floor is used."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"589969e0-25c9-4813-acd8-cf423be18f35","uuid":"6ef51bea-4f7d-4f61-9828-a7e0c8ccd4ea","timestamp":"2026-05-07T05:29:39.799Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/bbr.rs","content":"/// Under multipath each path has its own context; under single-path\n/// only the default path (`unique_path_id == 0`, corresponding to\n/// `cnx->path[0]` in C) participates in ECN tracking — other paths\n/// return `None`.\n///\n/// Note: in C the path held a back-pointer to its connection\n/// (`path_x->cnx`); in Rust there is no back-pointer, so the caller\n/// must supply both `connection` and `path_x`.\npub fn access_ecn_packet_context<'a>(\n    connection: &'a Connection,\n    path_x: &'a Path,\n) -> Option<&'a PacketContextState> {\n    if connection.is_multipath_enabled {\n        Some(&path_x.pkt_ctx)\n    } else if path_x.unique_path_id != 0 {\n        // Non-default path in single-path mode: ECN counts are not\n        // tracked per-path here; the caller should use the default path.\n        None\n    } else {\n        Some(&connection.pkt_ctx[PacketContext::Application as usize])\n    }\n}\n\n/// C: `BBRSetRsFromAckState` (picoquic/bbr.c:2363)\n///\n/// Convert the `PerAckState` delivered by picoquic's ACK-processing\n/// layer into the `BbrPerAckState` (\"rs\") struct used throughout BBRv3.\n/// Delivery rate is taken from the path's bandwidth estimate when\n/// available; otherwise it is derived from bytes-delivered / RTT; as a\n/// last resort a 40 kBps floor is used.","numLines":30,"startLine":870,"totalLines":1451}}}
